WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:16.517 --> 00:00:18.018
They said he was out
the door in two weeks.


00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:19.853
Then I hear the guy's
re-upped for five years.


00:00:19.937 --> 00:00:20.938
The label hated it.


00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.315
This castle belongs to
the Duke of Gloucester.


00:00:23.398 --> 00:00:26.735
So I realize that was the guy who kept
angrily staring at me the whole time.


00:00:26.819 --> 00:00:28.571
Hey, Kevin. Hey, Lorne.


00:00:28.654 --> 00:00:30.280
- You ready for this?
- Yeah, what's that?


00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.865
Oh, oh! We're gonna do the thing.
Okay.


00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:33.158
All right, you want to start it off?


00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:35.703
- Talk to you, or talk to the lens?
- Either way.


00:00:36.579 --> 00:00:38.914
So, Sandy Wexler...


00:00:42.209 --> 00:00:43.752
Where do I begin?


00:00:43.836 --> 00:00:46.088
He may be the most
unique guy I ever met.


00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:49.717
If you were working in Los Angeles
in the '90s, any time in there,


00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.259
you'd run into Sandy Wexler
at some point.


00:00:51.343 --> 00:00:53.637
Sandy was one of those
fringe Hollywood managers


00:00:53.721 --> 00:00:55.430
that you always sort of saw around.


00:00:55.513 --> 00:01:00.102
You know, you'd see him at a wrap party,
and he'd be laughing, stuffing his face.


00:01:00.185 --> 00:01:02.730
You'd think,
"No one even invited this guy."


00:01:02.813 --> 00:01:05.733
Sandy said I could be
the next Patrick Swayze.


00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:08.151
Only thing he ever said to me
that made sense.


00:01:08.235 --> 00:01:12.155
Sandy was not a big shot.
He was a... He was a tiny shot.


00:01:12.239 --> 00:01:16.534
But anybody who met him,
you never forgot him.


00:01:16.619 --> 00:01:19.747
You know, you gotta remember there
was no YouTube, there was no Vines.


00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.707
And none of that...
None of the social media platforms.


00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.834
You really needed a guy
like Sandy to be seen.


00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:28.130
Not Sandy.
Not Sandy, but a guy like Sandy.


00:01:57.575 --> 00:02:02.247
Hey, Arsenio!
Nice to see you again, kiddo.


00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:03.749
Have I seen you before?


00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:06.334
Yeah, it's Sandy Wexler.


00:02:06.418 --> 00:02:10.213
I met you at Bernie's beach house,
with Doug and Danny.


00:02:10.297 --> 00:02:12.174
You guys were playing hangman.


00:02:12.257 --> 00:02:16.219
You were hysterical that night. No one
could figure out the word "canoe."


00:02:17.179 --> 00:02:19.056
I have no idea
what you're talking about, man.


00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.725
How you doing with your manager, kid?
Are you still fighting?


00:02:22.392 --> 00:02:23.727
I don't have a manager, man.


00:02:23.811 --> 00:02:26.354
Well, you do now. If you want one.


00:02:26.438 --> 00:02:28.106
No, I'm good. I... I have an agent.


00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:30.025
- Oh.
- As a matter of fact, I have six agents.


00:02:30.108 --> 00:02:31.234
Got plenty of white people in my life.


00:02:31.318 --> 00:02:32.319
- All right.
- I'm good, dawg.


00:02:32.402 --> 00:02:36.448
An agent is business.
A manager is family.


00:02:36.531 --> 00:02:40.703
He guides you. He advises you.
He fights the good fights.


00:02:40.786 --> 00:02:42.329
Makes the tough phone calls.


00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:45.666
Truth is, I'm not happy unless...
unless you're happy.


00:02:45.749 --> 00:02:49.169
So what do you say, Arsenio?
You wanna get happy together?


00:02:51.379 --> 00:02:54.132
Continued success, Arsenio!


00:02:55.258 --> 00:02:57.761
Okay? Oh!


00:02:57.845 --> 00:03:00.513
I got a hit on the hip, and it's Sinbad.


00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:02.474
I don't think any of those people
were really beeping him.


00:03:02.557 --> 00:03:05.018
'Cause he would just go, like,
"Oh, jeez, Mackenzie Phillips."


00:03:05.102 --> 00:03:06.394
The one thing about Sandy is,


00:03:06.478 --> 00:03:09.189
- he just never stopped lying.
- Always.


00:03:09.272 --> 00:03:11.984
Managers get used to lying,
but Sandy took it to an art form.


00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:16.822
Where am I? I'm in Joel Silver's office
right now, talking about you.


00:03:16.905 --> 00:03:18.198
If you land on your feet...


00:03:18.281 --> 00:03:19.616
Hey, buddy, how long are you gonna be?


00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:22.870
Excuse me, I am talking
to Lew Wasserman's neighbor right now.


00:03:24.371 --> 00:03:26.832
That was Janet Maslin from the Times.


00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:28.125
Sandy's personal life?


00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:30.878
- I know nothing. I know nothing.
- Did he have a personal life?


00:03:30.961 --> 00:03:32.880
- He wasn't married.
- Didn't date.


00:03:32.963 --> 00:03:34.840
It was sad. Seemed like he
didn't have any friends, right?


00:03:34.923 --> 00:03:35.841
He had no friends.


00:03:41.096 --> 00:03:42.139
Any good?


00:03:46.769 --> 00:03:48.729
No, no, no, no, no, no.


00:03:52.357 --> 00:03:53.650
That's great.


00:03:55.402 --> 00:03:59.197
But he was the king of the fake laugh


00:03:59.281 --> 00:04:01.909
- and the applauding combo. Yeah.
- Combo. Yeah.


00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.247
Next time he'll get his own ketchup.


00:04:09.792 --> 00:04:10.793
You gotta go.


00:04:10.876 --> 00:04:13.003
Is Mary Jo Slater
the casting agent on this?


00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.379
- No. I don't know.
- Good job, guys.


00:04:14.462 --> 00:04:17.715
I was in Nam.
But, you know, I was there in 1984,


00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.427
so it was... It was a different vibe.


00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.598
And then all I hear in the back is...


00:04:29.019 --> 00:04:31.688
- He would fake laugh at funny comics.
- That melon.


00:04:31.772 --> 00:04:33.816
It was like, "Why are you fake laughing?


00:04:33.899 --> 00:04:35.567
- It's Eddie Murphy. He's funny."
- Right!


00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:38.153
When it came to eating
with Sandy, he, um...


00:04:38.236 --> 00:04:40.322
It was like a smorgasbord on his face.


00:04:40.405 --> 00:04:43.491
I mean, he was on the Atkins diet, right?
So he always had, like, chicken...


00:04:43.575 --> 00:04:45.202
- Kielbasa.
- T-bone steak.


00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.619
- Brisket.
- Beef jerky.


00:04:46.703 --> 00:04:49.622
I never actually ate with Sandy,
but I did hear it was kind of gross.


00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:53.335
Can you close your mouth
just a little bit?


00:04:55.462 --> 00:04:56.922
What did I do?


00:04:57.005 --> 00:04:59.842
He dressed like your grandfather,


00:04:59.925 --> 00:05:04.888
he had the table manners of a horse,
but he was a great manager.


00:05:04.972 --> 00:05:07.057
He really cared about his clients.


00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.893
He made them his family.
He was with them all the time.


00:05:09.977 --> 00:05:13.105
And, uh, I wasn't sure
what he was doing for them,


00:05:13.188 --> 00:05:14.189
but you could feel the love.


00:05:14.815 --> 00:05:18.986
I spoke to Chili's. I think I can
get us the corner table there


00:05:19.069 --> 00:05:20.570
and preorder the appetizers.


00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:22.239
I don't give a shit
about Chili's right now.


00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.824
I thought you wanted to go to Chili's.


00:05:23.907 --> 00:05:25.492
- No, I never said that.
- You said that.


00:05:25.575 --> 00:05:26.869
That's okay.


00:05:26.952 --> 00:05:29.329
You're nervous.
I can see that you're sweating.


00:05:29.412 --> 00:05:30.705
- I'm scared, Sandy.
- Yeah.


00:05:30.788 --> 00:05:32.916
I gotta jump over ten trailers
and land on a waterbed.


00:05:34.835 --> 00:05:36.086
Why are you laughing?


00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:38.130
Because you're funny.
You make me laugh.


00:05:38.213 --> 00:05:40.507
- Well, I'm not trying to be funny.
- No, it's the way you said it.


00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:42.425
The way I said...
What are you...


00:05:42.509 --> 00:05:44.094
Look at the size of this crowd.


00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:48.181
You said they'd come, and they came.


00:05:48.265 --> 00:05:53.436
Ladies and gentlemen
of El Segundo Motor Home Court,


00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.397
here to defy gravity,


00:05:55.480 --> 00:06:01.653
please let's welcome Wild Gary Roberts!


00:06:01.736 --> 00:06:03.738
- Rodgers!
- Rodgers!


00:06:05.448 --> 00:06:07.075
He said that. He said Rodgers.


00:06:07.159 --> 00:06:08.701
Yeah, 'cause I told him to!


00:06:08.785 --> 00:06:10.162
He said it the first time.


00:06:10.745 --> 00:06:14.541
I... I wish we could...
'Cause he did say it the first time.


00:06:14.624 --> 00:06:17.335
- Stop talking.
- All right. I will.


00:06:17.419 --> 00:06:19.963
You get up there
and you show these people who you are.


00:06:20.047 --> 00:06:22.049
Gary Rodgers.


00:06:22.132 --> 00:06:24.051
It's Gary Rodgers. You said that, right?


00:06:24.134 --> 00:06:25.177
The second time.


00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:26.761
Yeah, but you knew it.


00:06:26.844 --> 00:06:28.513
Okay, guys, let's do this.


00:06:38.773 --> 00:06:41.026
What are you saying?
I don't know what you're...


00:06:43.445 --> 00:06:46.489
What are you pointing to?
I can only go forward.


00:06:50.868 --> 00:06:52.412
Oh, my God.


00:06:52.996 --> 00:06:55.498
He's really gonna jump
over all those trailers?


00:06:55.582 --> 00:06:58.835
Sir, my client is the best daredevil
trapeze artist in the world.


00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:00.003
Thank you very much.


00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:02.672
Let's go.


00:07:03.631 --> 00:07:04.549
Yeah!


00:07:05.383 --> 00:07:06.969
What?


00:07:10.722 --> 00:07:12.182
...Oh, shit!


00:07:12.265 --> 00:07:14.809
Jesus Christ!


00:07:15.727 --> 00:07:16.979
Sandy.


00:07:18.355 --> 00:07:20.523
- He had this one guy, Ted Rafferty...
- Oh, yeah.


00:07:20.607 --> 00:07:23.526
...who was a, you know, puppet act.
Not that good. Like, a middle act.


00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:25.612
He believed in him.
He thought he was the greatest.


00:07:25.695 --> 00:07:28.323
He's like, "I'm gonna make him
the next Mr. Buttons."


00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:33.036
So, uh, Charlie,
have you always been a puppet?


00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.039
Well, I don't know.
Have you always been a parade float?


00:07:37.665 --> 00:07:39.834
I'm just trying
to get to know you better, that's all.


00:07:39.917 --> 00:07:42.170
Know me better?
I'm sitting on your lap.


00:07:43.505 --> 00:07:45.715
No, but seriously,
what's it like being a puppet?


00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:47.592
Well, I come from
a long line of puppets.


00:07:47.675 --> 00:07:51.179
My father was a puppet.
My father's father was a puppet.


00:07:51.263 --> 00:07:53.890
Really? Was your father's father's
father a puppet?


00:07:56.393 --> 00:07:58.686
Wait for the punch line, buddy.


00:08:01.523 --> 00:08:05.360
Somebody call JCPenney.
One of the mannequins is on the loose.


00:08:08.071 --> 00:08:09.781
Sir, have you ever had
a date in your life?


00:08:09.864 --> 00:08:11.408
Actually, I have.


00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:13.785
Your Anita Bryant poster doesn't count.


00:08:17.872 --> 00:08:20.625
But honestly, sir,
how long have you been dead for?


00:08:25.213 --> 00:08:29.176
Where do you come up with this stuff?
I wish you didn't.


00:08:29.259 --> 00:08:31.011
That was hysterical.


00:08:31.094 --> 00:08:32.387
So you caught the whole show, then?


00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:35.182
I saw every word of it.
It was sensational.


00:08:35.265 --> 00:08:36.766
I saw you come in late!


00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:39.394
Nah. Nah, I was there the whole time.


00:08:39.477 --> 00:08:41.188
Will you get a load of this bullcrap.


00:08:41.271 --> 00:08:43.565
I was. I was.


00:08:43.648 --> 00:08:45.567
Hey, hey, hey, hey,
now, guys, guys, please.


00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:47.319
All right. Sandy, I... I believe you.


00:08:47.402 --> 00:08:48.611
Thank you, Ted.


00:08:48.695 --> 00:08:53.158
And I was thinking, you'd do so well now
with the beach theater crowd.


00:08:53.241 --> 00:08:57.870
And you've got the once a month gig
opening for Fred Travalena at the Trop.


00:08:57.954 --> 00:08:59.456
I don't wanna lose that.


00:08:59.539 --> 00:09:02.042
It might be time
to move on to the next level.


00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:03.960
Kicking the piss out of you?


00:09:04.044 --> 00:09:06.838
No. Television.


00:09:07.964 --> 00:09:09.049
But...


00:09:09.132 --> 00:09:11.509
I don't know the first thing
about the TV business.


00:09:11.593 --> 00:09:12.677
That's why you got me.


00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:15.012
- I know my way around the networks.
- Liar!


00:09:15.097 --> 00:09:18.516
Hey, I've had a relationship
with CBS since 1965


00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.518
when I was a PA on Gilligan's Island.


00:09:20.602 --> 00:09:24.772
Now, look, kids love the puppets.
And I know there's an audience for that.


00:09:24.856 --> 00:09:26.191
Mmm, maybe.


00:09:27.109 --> 00:09:28.776
Well, what about this?


00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:32.447
I know it's out of left field,
but how about a show for kids?


00:09:33.156 --> 00:09:34.657
Yeah, I was just saying that.


00:09:34.741 --> 00:09:36.243
So we agree.


00:09:37.785 --> 00:09:40.288
My favorite thing about Sandy
is where he lived.


00:09:40.372 --> 00:09:41.914
The place was a palace.


00:09:41.998 --> 00:09:44.126
He lived
on the biggest property in Bel Air.


00:09:44.209 --> 00:09:45.210
Yeah.


00:09:45.293 --> 00:09:46.586
Gorgeous pool.


00:09:46.669 --> 00:09:49.631
One of the finest collections
of luxury cars I've ever seen.


00:09:50.215 --> 00:09:53.718
Make sure you hydrate, Yoshi!
It's a hot day!


00:09:56.554 --> 00:09:58.723
Of course, none of it belonged to Sandy.


00:09:58.806 --> 00:10:00.808
It was owned by some Jewish Iranian...


00:10:00.892 --> 00:10:03.936
The guy never even set foot
in the United States.


00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:06.356
...who needed Sandy there
for legal reasons.


00:10:06.439 --> 00:10:10.067
And he was not allowed
in the main house.


00:10:10.152 --> 00:10:12.737
He was in the cabana by the pool.


00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:15.907
...No, no, no, no.


00:10:17.033 --> 00:10:20.370
Oh, no! Oh, no, no!
No, no, no!


00:10:20.453 --> 00:10:22.372
Stay! Stay! Stay!


00:10:24.081 --> 00:10:28.253
I've lived here for four years already.
You should know me by now.


00:10:28.336 --> 00:10:30.963
Get to see the face.
The king of Hollywood.


00:10:31.047 --> 00:10:32.048
Do you understand me?


00:10:32.132 --> 00:10:33.550
- Sandy?
- Ahh!


00:10:34.759 --> 00:10:39.013
Oh. Hi, uh, Amy.
Hi, Donna and Kendra.


00:10:39.096 --> 00:10:40.640
- Lola.
- Jesse.


00:10:40.723 --> 00:10:44.144
Yeah, that's right.
Wow, they're getting sharp.


00:10:44.227 --> 00:10:47.104
What brings you all the way out here
from Tarzana?


00:10:47.189 --> 00:10:49.357
Well, you said you'd watch the kids
while I go on the audition.


00:10:49.441 --> 00:10:50.442
Is that still okay?


00:10:50.525 --> 00:10:56.364
Oh, don't be silly. Of course.
We're gonna have a good time, guys.


00:10:56.448 --> 00:10:57.532
I have to get it, Sandy.


00:10:57.615 --> 00:10:59.909
I'm working two jobs
just to tread water out here.


00:10:59.992 --> 00:11:04.747
You're the quintessential American mother.
Oscar Mayer would be crazy to pass on you.


00:11:04.831 --> 00:11:08.835
Oscar Mayer? I thought I was auditioning
to play a hooker in a Wes Craven movie.


00:11:08.918 --> 00:11:12.297
You know what? My doctor put me
on a new thyroid medicine.


00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:15.383
He said it might make me foggy,
and I guess he was right.


00:11:16.384 --> 00:11:17.927
- Okay, Sandy, I'm gonna go.
- Yeah.


00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:19.804
Girls, be nice to Mr. Wexler. Okay?


00:11:19.887 --> 00:11:20.888
Yes, Mommy.


00:11:20.972 --> 00:11:22.724
- Oh, we're gonna have fun, guys.
- Okay.


00:11:22.807 --> 00:11:24.976
- Go get 'em, kid. Go get 'em.
- Okay.


00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.937
Oh, there's dogs out there. They...


00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:32.442
Hey! Hi, guys. Hi, sweet girl. Hi.


00:11:33.401 --> 00:11:35.403
So what are you shmegegges up for?


00:11:35.487 --> 00:11:38.948
I have the original script
of On Golden Pond.


00:11:39.031 --> 00:11:41.033
Do you wanna read that out loud?


00:11:41.117 --> 00:11:42.159
No?


00:11:42.244 --> 00:11:43.661
What would you like to do?


00:11:43.745 --> 00:11:44.829
Go swimming?


00:11:44.912 --> 00:11:47.540
No, no, no.
That could get me kicked out of here.


00:11:47.624 --> 00:11:49.083
I thought you were
the king of Hollywood?


00:11:49.166 --> 00:11:50.252
I never said that.


00:11:50.335 --> 00:11:53.045
- You said it to the dogs.
- Like a minute ago.


00:11:53.129 --> 00:11:54.088
No, I didn't.


00:11:55.298 --> 00:11:57.717
You guys like roller coasters?


00:11:58.593 --> 00:12:00.803
Unbelievable.


00:12:00.887 --> 00:12:05.558
Rifkin left Triad and he's joining forces
with Zifkin over at William Morris.


00:12:05.642 --> 00:12:12.399
After I was promoted out of the mail-room
at MCA, I was assigned to Frank Gorshin.


00:12:12.482 --> 00:12:17.445
And Frank Gorshin used to have me
hand-wash the Riddler costume,


00:12:17.529 --> 00:12:22.784
because he felt washing machines
might stretch out the material.


00:12:24.118 --> 00:12:27.622
Hey, guys, this way.
This way. Come with me.


00:12:29.291 --> 00:12:32.084
♪ All through the wintertime ♪


00:12:32.168 --> 00:12:35.297
♪ He hid himself away ♪


00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:38.425
♪ Ashamed to show his face ♪


00:12:38.508 --> 00:12:41.177
♪ Afraid of what others might say ♪


00:12:41.969 --> 00:12:47.809
♪ All through the winter
In his lonely clump of leaves ♪


00:12:47.892 --> 00:12:51.062
- Hey, dude, I can't see.
- What? Okay.


00:12:51.145 --> 00:12:56.067
♪ And very soon agreed
Indeed ♪


00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:59.321
Yes, a very fine swan indeed.


00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:03.282
Take a look at yourself in the lake.
You'll see.


00:13:03.366 --> 00:13:05.827
♪ I'm not such an ugly duckling ♪


00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:09.414
♪ No feathers all stubby and brown ♪


00:13:09.497 --> 00:13:11.207
Pitch perfect.


00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:16.546
♪ In so many words
Say the best in town ♪


00:13:16.629 --> 00:13:18.172
♪ The best ♪


00:13:18.255 --> 00:13:19.924
♪ The best ♪


00:13:20.007 --> 00:13:21.343
♪ The best in town ♪


00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:24.387
Very nice.


00:13:25.137 --> 00:13:27.515
Excuse me.
You were fantastic up there.


00:13:27.599 --> 00:13:29.601
- Oh, thanks. You're sweet.
- Yeah.


00:13:29.684 --> 00:13:30.893
It's corny, but it's fun.


00:13:30.977 --> 00:13:33.730
