I don't know, I'm just smiling at the fact
you might become the new Captain Kangaroo.


00:25:48.464 --> 00:25:49.840
He's lying again.


00:25:49.923 --> 00:25:51.467
No, I'm not. I'm not lying.


00:25:51.550 --> 00:25:55.679
I've been thinking about how you
can work on your kid-friendly material.


00:25:55.762 --> 00:25:57.306
Maybe go to Magic Mountain.


00:25:57.389 --> 00:26:00.184
When you see all the children on line,
just start doing jokes for 'em.


00:26:00.267 --> 00:26:02.561
- See if it works.
- That feels very child molestery.


00:26:02.644 --> 00:26:05.106
He wants to ruin you. Fire him!


00:26:05.189 --> 00:26:07.399
Fire me?
If you're firing anybody, I'd fire him.


00:26:07.483 --> 00:26:09.151
He's useless. He does nothing.


00:26:09.235 --> 00:26:11.112
I do everything! What do you do?


00:26:11.195 --> 00:26:13.155
Guys, guys, guys!
Come on, we're on the same team here.


00:26:13.239 --> 00:26:15.073
- That's what I'm trying to tell him.
- Yes.


00:26:15.157 --> 00:26:16.367
Teammates?


00:26:17.284 --> 00:26:18.535
Yeah, thank you.


00:26:19.911 --> 00:26:23.081
- You took my arm! You took my arm!
- Oh, come off it. That's...


00:26:23.165 --> 00:26:25.126
- You took my arm!
- That's not...


00:26:25.209 --> 00:26:26.835
Thank you, Martin.


00:26:26.918 --> 00:26:31.257
Let's find out who the judges chose
as returning champ tonight.


00:26:31.840 --> 00:26:35.594
The judges gave Kevin Connors one star


00:26:35.677 --> 00:26:39.264
and the champion,
Martin Lawrence, four stars!


00:26:39.348 --> 00:26:41.057
The new champion, Martin Lawrence.


00:26:42.267 --> 00:26:45.187
...Oh... Come on.


00:26:45.979 --> 00:26:47.314
Wexler Artists.


00:26:47.398 --> 00:26:49.275
- It's me.
- Hi, Kevin.


00:26:49.358 --> 00:26:50.401
Did you know that was on?


00:26:50.484 --> 00:26:52.944
No. I didn't know
they were gonna repeat it.


00:26:53.028 --> 00:26:54.613
- I never want to see that again!
- Well...


00:26:54.696 --> 00:26:58.784
I can't stop them, Kevin, legally,
'cause we signed an agreement.


00:26:58.867 --> 00:27:00.619
It's... They own the material.


00:27:19.221 --> 00:27:21.432
Well, she'd light up a room
in that purple one.


00:27:31.900 --> 00:27:32.984
Sandy!


00:27:33.527 --> 00:27:35.487
Barry Bubatzi.


00:27:36.154 --> 00:27:37.155
Barry.


00:27:37.989 --> 00:27:40.826
Yeah, I was Carr D'Angelo's assistant?


00:27:41.410 --> 00:27:44.288
- Hiccups? That's you?
- Yeah.


00:27:44.371 --> 00:27:46.915
- Look at this. Hiccups.
- Yeah.


00:27:46.998 --> 00:27:48.292
Bubatzi!


00:27:48.375 --> 00:27:50.043
He... he called me Hiccups


00:27:50.126 --> 00:27:52.588
because I had the hiccups this one time
I was on the phone with him.


00:27:52.671 --> 00:27:54.381
Well, listen,
he didn't just have the hiccups,


00:27:54.465 --> 00:27:55.757
he had the hiccups.


00:27:55.841 --> 00:27:57.676
- He wouldn't stop hiccupping.
- Yeah.


00:27:57.759 --> 00:28:01.222
Uh, you can die from hiccups.
I was terrified.


00:28:01.305 --> 00:28:02.973
I was actually concerned.


00:28:03.056 --> 00:28:06.268
...It was nerve-racking. A little bit.


00:28:06.352 --> 00:28:09.438
How's your sister?
Did she get into Penn State?


00:28:09.521 --> 00:28:12.649
- She just graduated.
- Another successful Bubatzi.


00:28:12.733 --> 00:28:16.612
- You see, that is why I love this guy.
- What?


00:28:16.695 --> 00:28:20.115
He actually talked to me
when I was just an assistant.


00:28:20.198 --> 00:28:22.200
You treated me with respect, Sandy.


00:28:22.284 --> 00:28:23.827
- Not many people did.
- Well, of course.


00:28:23.910 --> 00:28:25.829
- This is my girl, Mary.
- Hi.


00:28:25.912 --> 00:28:27.122
Mary. Sandy Wexler.


00:28:27.205 --> 00:28:28.374
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.


00:28:28.457 --> 00:28:29.833
Are you...
What happened to your arm?


00:28:30.584 --> 00:28:34.588
- Yeah, I got myself a tattoo.
- What'd you get?


00:28:34.671 --> 00:28:37.716
Uh... it is that of a dog bite.


00:28:39.218 --> 00:28:41.094
So how's Carr D'Angelo?


00:28:41.177 --> 00:28:44.139
Well, he, uh... he left.
He's working for Blockbuster Video now.


00:28:44.723 --> 00:28:48.352
Smart move. The music business
has its ups and downs,


00:28:48.435 --> 00:28:51.438
but Blockbuster Video's here
for the long haul.


00:28:52.105 --> 00:28:54.190
And you, what are you up to?


00:28:54.275 --> 00:28:55.484
I left, too.


00:28:55.567 --> 00:28:57.778
- I'm at Capitol Records now.
- Oh.


00:28:57.861 --> 00:28:59.238
He's head of A&R.


00:29:00.364 --> 00:29:02.574
You know how happy that makes me?


00:29:02.658 --> 00:29:05.035
Hiccups Bubatzi goes big time.


00:29:05.118 --> 00:29:07.579
That's just...
That's the way it should be.


00:29:07.663 --> 00:29:09.831
You worked your ass off, kiddo.


00:29:09.915 --> 00:29:12.501
Can I talk business for a second?
Is that all right?


00:29:12.584 --> 00:29:14.628
I have a client that, actually,
you would love to meet...


00:29:14.711 --> 00:29:15.962
- Tell you what...
- What?


00:29:16.046 --> 00:29:19.550
Call my office next week. Yeah.


00:29:19.633 --> 00:29:21.843
I mean, you sure? 'Cause I will call.


00:29:21.927 --> 00:29:23.970
I know.


00:29:24.054 --> 00:29:25.764
- It was great seeing you, pal.
- It was great seeing you.


00:29:25.847 --> 00:29:28.267
And I hope, uh,
one of those dresses works out for you.


00:29:28.350 --> 00:29:30.436
- Oh, no, this isn't...
- Cute.


00:29:30.519 --> 00:29:32.604
- It was... I mean...
- So good.


00:29:33.188 --> 00:29:35.774
It's a Bubatzi world. We're all just...


00:29:35.857 --> 00:29:37.818
Could you please
not block the whole aisle?


00:29:38.777 --> 00:29:40.195
We're all just living in it.


00:29:40.279 --> 00:29:41.655
I wasn't blocking the aisle.


00:29:47.369 --> 00:29:48.454
Wow.


00:29:51.164 --> 00:29:53.041
- Hi.
- Hey, neighbor.


00:29:53.124 --> 00:29:54.960
Hi, Cindy!


00:29:55.043 --> 00:29:57.212
Where's that
billionaire landlord of yours?


00:29:57.296 --> 00:29:59.506
Is he ever going to grace us
with his presence?


00:29:59.590 --> 00:30:01.425
What a question.


00:30:01.508 --> 00:30:04.177
Listen, he's supposed to come out
for Rosh Hashanah,


00:30:04.260 --> 00:30:06.179
but he said last year Purim,
so who knows?


00:30:06.262 --> 00:30:08.223
...But anyways, how are you?


00:30:08.307 --> 00:30:09.600
How is your husband?


00:30:10.642 --> 00:30:12.728
Doctors say it could be
any day now. Hmm.


00:30:12.811 --> 00:30:15.564
Oh, I'm so sorry. It's just...


00:30:16.147 --> 00:30:18.609
How are you doing?
No one ever asks how you're doing.


00:30:18.692 --> 00:30:19.693
How you feeling?


00:30:20.276 --> 00:30:22.195
The truth is that I'm just...


00:30:22.904 --> 00:30:24.155
a little bit lonely.


00:30:24.239 --> 00:30:27.493
You were together so long.
Of course you're lonely.


00:30:27.576 --> 00:30:30.161
So if you ever see
my tennis court lights on at night...


00:30:31.287 --> 00:30:33.374
that means that I could
use some company.


00:30:36.877 --> 00:30:40.464
- It was great to see you, Cindy.
- Bye, Sandy.


00:30:41.089 --> 00:30:44.134
Okay, we're gonna go.
All right. Good night, now.


00:30:44.217 --> 00:30:45.552
Good night.


00:30:45.636 --> 00:30:48.389
Look, Gary Rodgers can't make that jump


00:30:48.472 --> 00:30:51.892
unless you clear
every bird from the sky, Tom.


00:30:54.811 --> 00:30:58.399
I don't know. Is there a spray for it?
Like, a... a roach spray or...


00:30:58.482 --> 00:31:00.275
There's dogs. There's dogs.


00:31:00.359 --> 00:31:02.277
A roach spray for birds.


00:31:03.111 --> 00:31:06.865
Tom, I'm sorry.
That's not my job. That's your job.


00:31:06.948 --> 00:31:08.909
That's why I'm telling you.


00:31:08.992 --> 00:31:10.327
I'm telling ya!


00:31:10.994 --> 00:31:14.205
Listen, don't do that to me!
I'll pull the plug on this thing!


00:31:14.289 --> 00:31:15.874
Do you hear me?


00:31:17.418 --> 00:31:20.629
All right. I'm sorry I got hot there,
Tom, but you weren't listening.


00:31:20.712 --> 00:31:24.340
Okay, here's a stock tip
for you to make up for that.


00:31:24.425 --> 00:31:26.718
Pull all your money out of Apple,


00:31:26.802 --> 00:31:28.887
'cause no one's using
the Macintosh anymore.


00:31:28.970 --> 00:31:35.351
Put 80% into small local bookstores,
the other 20% into Woolworth's.


00:31:36.269 --> 00:31:38.271
Righto.


00:31:38.397 --> 00:31:41.775
- Look at you, Mr. Manager Man.
- You don't wanna yell at people,


00:31:41.858 --> 00:31:43.944
but sometimes
it's the only way they can hear.


00:31:44.027 --> 00:31:45.111
You look stunning.


00:31:45.195 --> 00:31:50.451
Well, this yard is the most amazing yard
I've ever seen, and that pool...


00:31:50.534 --> 00:31:52.327
The pool's off-limits. House rules.


00:31:52.411 --> 00:31:54.788
So, Yuri stopped by my office.


00:31:54.871 --> 00:31:57.583
Yeah, I know. He's right there.


00:31:59.918 --> 00:32:02.754
You see him? Let's go over.


00:32:03.714 --> 00:32:06.508
We need to find the one
that expresses the right message.


00:32:06.592 --> 00:32:09.636
You know, "I'm fun.
I'm complicated. I'm sexy."


00:32:09.720 --> 00:32:11.930
I'm confused. I'm crazy.
I'm embarrassed.


00:32:12.013 --> 00:32:14.475
You're beautiful is what you are.
Stop that.


00:32:14.558 --> 00:32:17.060
...Got a hit on the hip.


00:32:17.143 --> 00:32:19.813
This is someone I actually have to call.


00:32:20.856 --> 00:32:22.816
Okay, I'll be back in a few seconds.


00:32:22.899 --> 00:32:24.568
Okay, cool, we'll be in the pool.


00:32:25.235 --> 00:32:26.653
You stay out of the pool.


00:32:26.737 --> 00:32:27.904
I was just kidding.


00:32:28.530 --> 00:32:30.824
I know, and it was hysterical.


00:32:30.907 --> 00:32:32.743
But seriously, stay out of the pool.


00:32:32.826 --> 00:32:34.911
No, not you, Barry. Hi!


00:32:36.663 --> 00:32:39.124
- I don't know how you do it.
- Do what?


00:32:39.750 --> 00:32:42.043
Deal with all the crazy Sandy shit.


00:32:42.127 --> 00:32:45.130
- Man, he's such a...
- Boner face?


00:32:45.213 --> 00:32:47.716
- I love that.
- He's not a boner face.


00:32:47.799 --> 00:32:49.676
- He's a badass.
- Okay.


00:32:50.511 --> 00:32:53.597
Well, listen, this girl is one
of the best singers you'll ever see,


00:32:53.680 --> 00:32:56.016
and the best, brightest person ever.


00:32:56.099 --> 00:32:59.853
I'm gonna go with the one
on the top right corner.


00:33:00.521 --> 00:33:03.356
And can you blow up... that one?


00:33:04.232 --> 00:33:05.567
Oh, my God.


00:33:05.651 --> 00:33:07.152
What? It's a good picture.


00:33:07.235 --> 00:33:09.613
Sandy already asked me
to do that for him.


00:33:12.866 --> 00:33:14.701
I have some interesting news.


00:33:14.785 --> 00:33:18.079
Capitol Records wants
to meet with you next week.


00:33:18.163 --> 00:33:19.831
They want to hear your demo.


00:33:21.207 --> 00:33:22.751
I don't have a demo.


00:33:22.834 --> 00:33:24.878
That's why you have me.


00:33:27.130 --> 00:33:31.677
♪ You make it feel like home ♪


00:33:31.760 --> 00:33:38.183
♪ You give me butterflies, butterflies
Down to my soul ♪


00:33:38.767 --> 00:33:43.188
♪ Butterfly, butterfly
You don't even know ♪


00:33:43.271 --> 00:33:49.778
♪ It's you who I speak of
And you who I dream of ♪


00:33:49.861 --> 00:33:55.867
♪ And nights when I'm all alone ♪


00:33:55.951 --> 00:34:01.331
♪ You make it feel like home ♪


00:34:06.377 --> 00:34:09.380
Courtney, one take. Perfection.


00:34:10.215 --> 00:34:12.300
You nailed it. That was...


00:34:13.218 --> 00:34:14.761
Thank you so much.


00:34:14.844 --> 00:34:17.138
I'm gonna play this back in here.


00:34:17.931 --> 00:34:20.809
I can't get over what I just heard. Wow.


00:34:20.892 --> 00:34:21.935
My God.


00:34:22.894 --> 00:34:26.272
Play it back. I...
I don't even know what to say right now.


00:34:27.232 --> 00:34:28.233
Uh...


00:34:31.570 --> 00:34:34.197
There's a chance I forgot to hit record.


00:34:35.198 --> 00:34:37.492
What do you mean
there's a chance you forgot?


00:34:37.576 --> 00:34:39.703
- I... I was gonna hit record...
- Uh-huh.


00:34:40.871 --> 00:34:42.163
Uh, then I forgot.


00:34:43.456 --> 00:34:44.833
So it's more than a chance.


00:34:44.916 --> 00:34:47.418
- You... you did forget?
- Yes.


00:34:48.003 --> 00:34:50.756
Okay, so what do we do now?


00:34:50.839 --> 00:34:53.800
Is it another deck you have?
Is it in the board?


00:34:53.884 --> 00:34:55.135
No.


00:34:55.218 --> 00:34:58.639
- So we'll have to do it again.
- Okay.


00:34:59.222 --> 00:35:01.224
Okay? It's okay with you?


00:35:01.307 --> 00:35:03.685
If it's okay with you to do it again.


00:35:03.769 --> 00:35:06.187
- That's where we are right now, huh?
- Okay.


00:35:06.271 --> 00:35:07.522
Let's just go again.


00:35:10.275 --> 00:35:14.112
Courtney, there was an issue
on the subwoofer.


00:35:14.195 --> 00:35:15.571
It was a bit tinny.


00:35:15.656 --> 00:35:18.283
We adjusted that,
and we're ready for you this time.


00:35:18.366 --> 00:35:22.162
I'm sorry. On us, not you.
Just one more time.


00:35:22.245 --> 00:35:25.581
We're gonna keep our eyes
on the road. Okay?


00:35:25.666 --> 00:35:26.917
You got it.


00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:29.753
Please promise me
it's as good as your first one.


00:35:29.836 --> 00:35:31.963
I'm... Ha!


00:35:32.047 --> 00:35:34.800
You know... You know you can do that.
Okay. All right.


00:35:35.383 --> 00:35:36.802
Go get 'em, kiddo.


00:35:41.181 --> 00:35:45.769
♪ Once in a while
You find someone ♪


00:35:46.978 --> 00:35:53.902
♪ I dream of
At nights when I'm all alone ♪


00:35:54.820 --> 00:36:00.450
♪ You make it feel like home ♪


00:36:02.744 --> 00:36:07.666
I am so happy we had another take,
because that just killed me.


00:36:07.749 --> 00:36:09.751
It was so on the money.


00:36:09.835 --> 00:36:12.879
You were hitting notes
I didn't know were invented yet.


00:36:12.963 --> 00:36:16.091
Thank you from the bottom of my heart.
I'm gonna take a listen.


00:36:22.638 --> 00:36:24.557
God damn it!


00:36:26.476 --> 00:36:28.687
I should have known
you would never press the button.


00:36:28.770 --> 00:36:31.481
You didn't remember to put the button
on your goddamn overalls!


00:36:38.238 --> 00:36:39.698
Is everything okay out there?


00:36:40.406 --> 00:36:43.785
Yes, kiddo,
we are doing just fine. Um...


00:36:44.745 --> 00:36:47.831
We need to go one last time.
There was a glitch.


00:36:47.914 --> 00:36:53.669
There was a tremolo-treble-bass hiccup
that we have rectified,


00:36:53.754 --> 00:36:55.463
and we're ready for ya.


00:36:55.546 --> 00:36:58.925
Take three it is.
Three time's the charm. Ha!


00:36:59.009 --> 00:37:01.386
- Okay, kiddo, let's hit 'em.
- Okay.


00:37:03.513 --> 00:37:05.681
It's not rolling. It's not rolling.


00:37:06.516 --> 00:37:08.059
Press the button!


00:37:09.227 --> 00:37:13.314
Push it! It's spinning, right?!


00:37:13.398 --> 00:37:19.029
♪ Butterflies, butterflies
Down to my soul ♪


00:37:19.112 --> 00:37:22.824
♪ Butterfly, butterfly
You don't even know ♪


00:37:22.908 --> 00:37:29.330
I mean, it's... it's like a bird
and an angel and a saxophone


00:37:29.414 --> 00:37:31.666
- made love and had a baby.
- Oh, wow.


00:37:32.583 --> 00:37:38.799
I'm also hearing a triangle
just between all the choruses.


00:37:38.882 --> 00:37:40.550
How can you hear a shape?


00:37:40.633 --> 00:37:41.885
The instrument!


00:37:43.011 --> 00:37:44.012
Just...


00:37:44.095 --> 00:37:45.972
♪ Butterflies ♪


00:37:48.433 --> 00:37:50.185
♪ Butterflies ♪


00:37:51.561 --> 00:37:53.438
And then it would be perfect.


00:37:53.521 --> 00:37:55.816
Really? A triangle?


00:37:56.524 --> 00:37:57.943
You don't think that will sound corny?


00:37:58.026 --> 00:38:00.570
Way in the back. Just barely audible.


00:38:00.653 --> 00:38:05.909
♪ You make it feel like home ♪


00:38:17.003 --> 00:38:19.505
These guys get...


00:38:21.299 --> 00:38:25.095
Sandy, um, my dad wanted to make sure
that I said hi to you.


00:38:25.178 --> 00:38:26.596
- Your father, Marty?
- Yeah.


00:38:26.679 --> 00:38:29.557
Say hi for me.
He's a good man. A smart man.


00:38:29.640 --> 00:38:33.603
Um, he felt bad that you didn't get
into Hillcrest Country Club this year.


00:38:33.686 --> 00:38:38.024
Oh, listen, that's not his fault. I was...
That was fine. There's other clubs.


00:38:38.108 --> 00:38:41.027
No, actually I think
that his was the deciding vote.


00:38:41.111 --> 00:38:44.697
No. It's a capacity thing.
It's not his fault. It's...


00:38:44.780 --> 00:38:45.824
Let's do the meeting.


00:38:45.907 --> 00:38:48.368
- All right. We're glad you're here.
- Okay. Good.


00:38:48.451 --> 00:38:50.786
So anyway, now that we got
the formalities out of the way...


00:38:50.871 --> 00:38:53.706
Everybody got their Fruitopia?
Good, good, good.


00:38:53.789 --> 00:38:55.291
So, spoke to Barry.


00:38:55.375 --> 00:38:57.543
And, uh, Barry wanted us
to listen to your demo,


00:38:57.627 --> 00:38:59.754
and I gotta say, some good stuff there.


00:38:59.838 --> 00:39:00.839
Thank you.


00:39:00.922 --> 00:39:04.425
Just to... I mean, to me, no one's doing
what this kid is doing out there.


00:39:04.509 --> 00:39:06.761
It's... it's not Mariah.
It's not Whitney. It's...


00:39:06.845 --> 00:39:09.264
Well, listen, if she got the album sales
of Whitney, we'll take it.


00:39:09.347 --> 00:39:10.431
...Oh. Well, no,


00:39:10.515 --> 00:39:13.434
in terms of sound
and commerciability, absolutely.


00:39:13.518 --> 00:39:15.854
It's definitely Whitney.
It's a Whitney, 100%.


00:39:15.937 --> 00:39:17.480
- Yeah, it has potential.
- Well, hold on now.


00:39:17.563 --> 00:39:19.232
The production quality is complete shit.


00:39:19.315 --> 00:39:21.609
Complete shit. Terrible.


00:39:21.692 --> 00:39:25.321
But the song has potential.
Yeah, no diggity, no doubt.


00:39:25.405 --> 00:39:26.489
- Thank you.
- That's it.


00:39:26.572 --> 00:39:28.366
The song is all we're worried about.


00:39:28.449 --> 00:39:30.785
You gotta lose the corny triangle,
though, man.


00:39:32.037 --> 00:39:34.497
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
No, consider that gone.


00:39:34.580 --> 00:39:37.583
Let me ask you something, man.
Whose insane idea was that, anyway?


