Uh... no, the address is in Bel Air.


00:52:38.698 --> 00:52:41.867
Oh, so he moved? Okay, okay, he moved.


00:52:55.547 --> 00:52:57.842
Sandy Wexler. Wow.


00:52:57.925 --> 00:52:59.468
They let you in this party?


00:52:59.551 --> 00:53:00.803
Hey, Bronstein.


00:53:00.886 --> 00:53:02.847
You heard you didn't get into
Hillcrest Country Club, right?


00:53:02.930 --> 00:53:04.014
Yeah, I heard.


00:53:04.098 --> 00:53:06.809
This place is incredible!


00:53:06.892 --> 00:53:09.019
Yeah, it's nice. It's nice.


00:53:09.103 --> 00:53:11.438
His one in Venice wasn't trying as hard.


00:53:12.314 --> 00:53:14.649
Quincy never lived in Venice.
What you talking about, Willis?


00:53:14.734 --> 00:53:16.360
What? No, she said he did.


00:53:16.443 --> 00:53:19.321
- What?
- She? Oh!


00:53:19.404 --> 00:53:20.990
I'm a huge fan. I'm Arsenio.


00:53:21.656 --> 00:53:24.576
I know, Arsenio. Courtney.


00:53:24.659 --> 00:53:29.289
Hey, Arsenio. Good to see you.
I'm Sandy Wexler, her manager.


00:53:29.373 --> 00:53:32.459
You remember? We met at, uh...
at Bernie's beach house.


00:53:32.542 --> 00:53:35.337
Your manager look like he fell down
an elevator shaft. What's up?


00:53:35.420 --> 00:53:39.341
No, no, no. I, uh... Fender bender.
You should see the other guy.


00:53:39.424 --> 00:53:41.593
- Oh, he got hurt?
- Who did?


00:53:41.676 --> 00:53:44.054
- The other guy?
- What? No.


00:53:45.765 --> 00:53:48.183
You know what?
I heard your new song, "Mr. DJ."


00:53:48.267 --> 00:53:50.644
I love it. It's off the chain.
You've gotta come on the show and do it.


00:53:50.727 --> 00:53:52.479
- I would love to.
- Oh, well, listen.


00:53:52.562 --> 00:53:55.024
I got a call from Johnny Carson
today, actually.


00:53:55.107 --> 00:53:59.694
He heard the song as well on the radio,
and he booked her on the show next week.


00:53:59.779 --> 00:54:01.030
Carson?


00:54:02.197 --> 00:54:03.407
Well, congratulations.


00:54:03.490 --> 00:54:07.119
You ever need me, Stage 29.
I'll be there forever, baby.


00:54:07.202 --> 00:54:10.622
Ah, thanks, Arsenio.
No, I didn't mean any problem...


00:54:10.705 --> 00:54:13.375
You didn't tell me
I was doing Carson next week!


00:54:13.458 --> 00:54:17.087
That was a negotiation ploy.
I may have overplayed my hand there.


00:54:17.171 --> 00:54:18.755
Carson retired two years ago.


00:54:18.839 --> 00:54:21.050
Sandy Wexler?
Somebody hide the pastrami.


00:54:22.384 --> 00:54:24.219
Hey, thank you. Good to see you, too.


00:54:25.846 --> 00:54:29.224
Wow. Look at all these awards he has.


00:54:29.308 --> 00:54:30.684
You'll have more one day.


00:54:30.767 --> 00:54:32.769
- Me?
- Yes, you.


00:54:32.853 --> 00:54:33.979
You promise me this.


00:54:34.063 --> 00:54:36.523
- After you win your first Grammy...
- Uh-huh.


00:54:36.606 --> 00:54:40.485
...you go home that night, you
put your ugly duckling hat on...


00:54:40.569 --> 00:54:41.695
I am not putting that hat on.


00:54:41.778 --> 00:54:43.363
...to remind yourself
where you come from.


00:54:43.447 --> 00:54:46.658
- You put it on. I'm not putting it on.
- You don't wanna see me in that...


00:54:46.741 --> 00:54:48.869
Sandy, Sandy, Sandy.


00:54:49.453 --> 00:54:51.413
Well, who whooped your ass
and got away with it?


00:54:51.496 --> 00:54:56.501
No, this was a high-impact
Tae Bo class I took. It's fine.


00:54:56.585 --> 00:54:57.586
Okay.


00:54:57.669 --> 00:55:00.714
How about our girl here
getting the radio play, huh?


00:55:00.797 --> 00:55:02.757
Did I tell you she's
a superstar or what?


00:55:02.842 --> 00:55:04.468
Oh, yeah, she's getting some heat.


00:55:04.551 --> 00:55:06.803
- Yeah, we'll see where it goes.
- Thanks, Bling.


00:55:06.887 --> 00:55:11.433
Excuse me. Excuse me, Shortie Doo-Wop,
can I get two Zimas and for Sandy...


00:55:11.516 --> 00:55:13.435
I'll take a diet ginger ale.


00:55:13.518 --> 00:55:16.563
- Amy Baskin.
- Sandy, what are you doing here?


00:55:16.646 --> 00:55:19.859
I was invited.
Thank you very much. Hi.


00:55:20.567 --> 00:55:22.736
Bling, I want you to meet Amy Baskin.


00:55:22.819 --> 00:55:25.572
To me, she is the next Grace Kelly.


00:55:25.655 --> 00:55:28.242
- I'm trying.
- Amy? Courtney.


00:55:28.325 --> 00:55:29.743
Remember me from the ritual pool party?


00:55:29.826 --> 00:55:32.872
Oh, my God. I heard your song
on the radio twice today.


00:55:32.955 --> 00:55:36.000
- Congratulations, Courtney.
- Oh, well, we got a great manager.


00:55:36.083 --> 00:55:38.585
He told me to always
sing from the heart.


00:55:38.668 --> 00:55:41.171
And I tell this girl,
"Always act from the heart."


00:55:41.255 --> 00:55:43.883
Hey, did we get the offer on
the Mentos commercial I was on hold for?


00:55:43.966 --> 00:55:47.719
No, you weren't on hold for it.
What I said was,


00:55:47.802 --> 00:55:51.598
"I called them and they put me on hold
for about 45 minutes."


00:55:51.681 --> 00:55:55.185
But when they... they got on the phone,
they told me they passed on you.


00:55:56.353 --> 00:55:57.938
- Well, there you go.
- No, it's good.


00:55:58.022 --> 00:55:59.523
They said she had a great reading.


00:55:59.606 --> 00:56:02.026
That it truly looked like
she loved the Mentos.


00:56:02.859 --> 00:56:04.111
I'll be back with your drinks.


00:56:04.194 --> 00:56:05.195
- Okay.
- Okay.


00:56:05.279 --> 00:56:08.573
Yo, check it out. It's OJ Simpson,
Phil Spector and Robert Blake.


00:56:08.657 --> 00:56:11.493
Good guys.
Call 'em the dream team.


00:56:11.576 --> 00:56:13.162
- I'm gonna go chop it up with 'em.
- All right.


00:56:13.245 --> 00:56:16.123
The juice is on the loose!
What's happening, killer?


00:56:16.706 --> 00:56:20.252
So, uh, what do you think?
We've been to the party. We had fun.


00:56:20.335 --> 00:56:22.879
- Time to go?
- I wanna see Jonesy.


00:56:22.963 --> 00:56:25.299
- Who's Jonesy?
- Quincy?


00:56:25.382 --> 00:56:27.927
- Oh, Quincy? You wanna see, uh...
- Yeah.


00:56:28.010 --> 00:56:29.386
...Quincelius?


00:56:29.469 --> 00:56:30.887
All right. Let's get that done.


00:56:30.971 --> 00:56:33.307
- You think he's around?
- Yeah, it'll be good to see him again.


00:56:34.099 --> 00:56:35.434
Uh, yeah, let's find him.


00:56:36.143 --> 00:56:40.981
Okay, now, Courtney,
it's Domaines Ott Bandol Rosé.


00:56:41.065 --> 00:56:42.316
- My favorite.
- Mmm.


00:56:48.989 --> 00:56:50.324
What do you think?


00:56:50.407 --> 00:56:53.202
Mmm! This is so good, Mr. Jones.


00:56:53.285 --> 00:56:55.037
What do you think, Sandy?
You like it?


00:56:56.580 --> 00:56:57.998
What's the matter, man?


00:56:58.082 --> 00:57:00.125
Nothing. No, I think it's good.


00:57:00.209 --> 00:57:02.502
It's... it's... It's just grapey.


00:57:03.337 --> 00:57:07.716
- What do you mean "grapey"?
- Oh, I... I didn't say it was a bad thing.


00:57:08.717 --> 00:57:11.178
Okay. I'm gonna try
to respect your opinion, brother.


00:57:11.761 --> 00:57:15.515
Let me try another one. I've got
a '61 Château Pétrus downstairs.


00:57:15.599 --> 00:57:16.725
Okay.


00:57:16.808 --> 00:57:19.519
I paid eight grand for it
at the Côte de Nuits.


00:57:19.603 --> 00:57:21.396
- Yeah, okay.
- That's too much. No.


00:57:21.480 --> 00:57:23.690
Pretty sure this'll get your attention.


00:57:23.773 --> 00:57:25.400
Thank you, Quincelius.


00:57:25.484 --> 00:57:26.901
Who the hell is Quincelius?


00:57:27.819 --> 00:57:30.155
Nobody. Come on. What are we doing here?


00:57:33.075 --> 00:57:34.659
Thank you.


00:57:34.743 --> 00:57:36.954
It was grapey. It was a little grapey.


00:57:37.037 --> 00:57:40.624
- I think you offended him.
- No, I didn't.


00:57:40.707 --> 00:57:42.251
I thought it was cool.


00:57:43.293 --> 00:57:47.256
When he comes back, I dare you
to say you hate that one, too.


00:57:47.339 --> 00:57:48.507
What?


00:57:48.590 --> 00:57:51.843
The man spent $8,000 on the wine.
He'll kill me.


00:57:51.926 --> 00:57:54.638
Oh, we'll laugh our asses off. Come on.


00:57:54.721 --> 00:57:59.393
- Courtney, what do you got me doing here?
- I was saving this for a special occasion.


00:57:59.476 --> 00:58:01.270
I think this is special enough.


00:58:03.438 --> 00:58:05.732
You'll have to let me know
what you think, baby.


00:58:05.815 --> 00:58:07.567
Yeah. Thank you.


00:58:08.818 --> 00:58:09.944
Very much.


00:58:11.405 --> 00:58:13.032
What do you think, honey?


00:58:13.115 --> 00:58:16.326
Mr. Jones, this is exquisite.


00:58:16.410 --> 00:58:18.037
And, Sanford, you likey?


00:58:23.333 --> 00:58:25.919
- Honestly?
- What else, man?


00:58:27.462 --> 00:58:30.090
- It's a little nutty.
- Nutty?


00:58:31.341 --> 00:58:32.842
For my taste.


00:58:37.514 --> 00:58:40.017
Maybe if you put an ice cube in it...


00:58:40.100 --> 00:58:44.813
- Oh, my goodness.
- Get out of my house!


00:58:44.896 --> 00:58:46.273
- Now!
- Hey, hey, I didn't mean to...


00:58:48.400 --> 00:58:50.402
- Now! Out! Out!
- I'm gonna leave.


00:58:50.485 --> 00:58:53.072
- No, I just got to get my jacket.
- Out! Get... get out of here.


00:58:53.155 --> 00:58:54.781
- Listen.
- Out!


00:58:54.864 --> 00:58:58.202
Man, one of these is mine.
Is this navy or black?


00:58:58.285 --> 00:59:02.122
I'm having a hard time seeing.
My glasses are blurry from the wine toss.


00:59:02.206 --> 00:59:03.373
Get out!


00:59:03.457 --> 00:59:06.043
You know what? This is probably it.
I... I'm gonna go.


00:59:06.126 --> 00:59:08.837
- Leave!
- Courtney! Okay.


00:59:08.920 --> 00:59:12.049
Hey. Thank you, Q-bert.
It was a great night.


00:59:12.132 --> 00:59:15.135
- Did you see the way that was...
- You made me do that! You!


00:59:15.219 --> 00:59:16.511
- How are we getting out?
- Are you happy?


00:59:16.595 --> 00:59:18.930
I don't know where...
Go. Just go. Is he coming?


00:59:19.013 --> 00:59:22.892
Courtney's first single was huge.
I remember the album was even bigger.


00:59:22.976 --> 00:59:25.937
I heard every song
on every station of every radio.


00:59:30.650 --> 00:59:32.277
Yay, Courtney!


00:59:34.529 --> 00:59:37.116
Courtney blew up
to Whitney Houston-type status.


00:59:37.199 --> 00:59:38.200
Oh, really?


00:59:38.283 --> 00:59:39.951
- So it was crazy.
- Mariah Carey, you know...


00:59:44.331 --> 00:59:48.252
You're nobody, and then you're somebody,
and everyone's clamoring after you.


00:59:48.335 --> 00:59:50.837
And it's scary. It can be scary.


01:00:04.101 --> 01:00:06.520
- Sandy...
- Courtney, what's wrong?


01:00:06.603 --> 01:00:08.813
I think someone's outside my house.


01:00:08.897 --> 01:00:11.441
I'm scared it's one of those freaks
that's been calling me or something.


01:00:11.525 --> 01:00:13.610
What? Who's calling you?


01:00:13.693 --> 01:00:14.903
I don't know.


01:00:14.986 --> 01:00:17.781
I've been dealing with this
ever since I moved into this place.


01:00:17.864 --> 01:00:19.991
- Are your doors locked?
- Yeah.


01:00:20.074 --> 01:00:22.244
You stay inside. I'll be right there.


01:00:32.879 --> 01:00:34.589
You're in trouble now, tough guy!


01:00:35.424 --> 01:00:38.427
Look what I've been carrying
around in my backseat...


01:00:39.093 --> 01:00:42.139
ever since I was attacked
on Ventura Place.


01:00:43.056 --> 01:00:45.434
Huh? You like this?


01:00:46.143 --> 01:00:47.936
You wanna... You wanna feel it?


01:00:49.604 --> 01:00:51.148
Come out! Where are you?


01:00:52.316 --> 01:00:55.026
Courtney, stay in the house!


01:00:58.363 --> 01:00:59.531
What's that?


01:01:01.200 --> 01:01:03.285
What? You think you can hide?


01:01:05.954 --> 01:01:09.541
Are you scared? Huh?


01:01:09.624 --> 01:01:11.960
'Cause I'm scared, too.


01:01:12.043 --> 01:01:15.380
I'm scared I'm gonna shatter
every bone in your face!


01:01:22.346 --> 01:01:23.597
You're gone?


01:01:25.474 --> 01:01:28.185
That's it. Truce.


01:01:29.394 --> 01:01:30.395
No more.


01:01:35.817 --> 01:01:37.194
Ow!


01:01:41.615 --> 01:01:46.745
What you were so afraid of
was nothing but a raccoon.


01:01:46.828 --> 01:01:47.829
No way.


01:01:47.912 --> 01:01:51.208
I'm telling you, you'll never have to
worry about him again, though.


01:01:51.916 --> 01:01:53.627
You didn't kill him, did you?


01:01:54.503 --> 01:01:56.796
No. No. Uh, I...


01:01:56.880 --> 01:02:01.134
I seen him go out into the forest again
to see his family, so...


01:02:01.218 --> 01:02:02.886
All right? But I screamed at him.


01:02:02.969 --> 01:02:06.306
I let him know, "Don't come back here.
You stay with the...


01:02:07.474 --> 01:02:09.351
On your side of the fence."


01:02:09.434 --> 01:02:11.270
Okay.


01:02:11.353 --> 01:02:13.272
Come on in.
Let me wash those clothes.


01:02:13.355 --> 01:02:17.401
When I used to represent Hooch
from Turner & Hooch,


01:02:17.484 --> 01:02:21.738
I got a similar call
about a late-night trespasser.


01:02:21.821 --> 01:02:24.449
Turned out it was Benji's trainer.


01:02:24.533 --> 01:02:29.579
Uh, he was jealous that Hooch
was now the hottest dog in the business.


01:02:29.663 --> 01:02:32.707
- You're making that up.
- No, no, no, I think that's true.


01:02:32.791 --> 01:02:35.960
You're insane, Sandy.
Take off those pants.


01:02:36.711 --> 01:02:39.298
What? What, right here?


01:02:39.381 --> 01:02:40.424
I won't look.


01:02:40.507 --> 01:02:42.592
Well, you'll be missing out, then.


01:02:42.676 --> 01:02:44.344
Oh, really?


01:02:45.011 --> 01:02:47.221
No. Maybe you should turn around.


01:02:47.306 --> 01:02:49.766
Turning around.


01:02:49.849 --> 01:02:52.852
I'm glad you took
this place, by the way.


01:02:52.936 --> 01:02:54.688
The real estate lady told me


01:02:54.771 --> 01:02:58.567
that David Crosby died
three times in this house.


01:02:58.650 --> 01:03:00.902
I'm gonna keep the beeper,
if that's all right.


01:03:00.985 --> 01:03:03.738
Kevin Connors did
a show on Brea tonight,


01:03:03.822 --> 01:03:07.867
co-headlining with AJ Jamal.
I wanna make sure that went well.


01:03:08.827 --> 01:03:11.204
So, pants are coming down.


01:03:12.121 --> 01:03:13.373
Here you go.


01:03:15.792 --> 01:03:18.337
All right. Come on.
Let's get these washed.


01:03:18.920 --> 01:03:21.005
Sure. Hey, thanks for doing that.


01:03:24.884 --> 01:03:26.470
You called Bling, too?


01:03:26.553 --> 01:03:28.513
Oh, I was here anyway, Sandy.


01:03:28.597 --> 01:03:30.474
With my pants on.


01:03:35.144 --> 01:03:38.064
The important thing
is that Courtney feels safe.


01:03:38.147 --> 01:03:40.066
- That's all I'm worried about.
- Hmm.


01:03:40.149 --> 01:03:41.818
An unlisted phone number.


01:03:41.901 --> 01:03:43.737
That's the way to go
for an artist of your stature.


01:03:43.820 --> 01:03:45.780
I can get that done for you
tomorrow morning.


01:03:45.864 --> 01:03:49.075
Oh, no, it's all... It's all good,
Sandy. I handled it already.


01:03:49.158 --> 01:03:52.245
Oh, you did? Good. Good. Good for you.


01:03:55.164 --> 01:03:57.125
Sandy, can you pass me the gravy?


01:03:57.208 --> 01:04:00.712
Can I pass you the gravy?
Absolutely. I can pass you the gravy.


01:04:00.795 --> 01:04:02.547
- Here. You want me to put it on for you?
- I got it.


01:04:02.631 --> 01:04:03.923
- You got it?
- Yeah.


01:04:04.007 --> 01:04:06.760
I was thinking we should get back
in the studio, Courtney.


01:04:06.843 --> 01:04:09.262
Maybe noodle around with some new tunes.


01:04:09.346 --> 01:04:11.973
With all due respect, Sandy,
I understand that,


01:04:12.056 --> 01:04:15.268
but, uh, her existing record's
gonna be on the charts for months.


01:04:15.352 --> 01:04:17.604
You don't want her competing
against herself now, do you?


01:04:17.687 --> 01:04:21.733
Who else do you want her competing with?
I mean it's a win-win. To me.


01:04:24.318 --> 01:04:25.570
I know what you mean, Sandy.


01:04:25.654 --> 01:04:28.865
I have lots of ideas,
but I can't tomorrow.


01:04:28.948 --> 01:04:31.075
We've got publicist meetings.


01:04:31.159 --> 01:04:34.371
- Publicists? What... what publicists?
- Oh, yeah, just the top ones.


01:04:34.454 --> 01:04:36.039
You know what?
I'll send you the list, actually.


01:04:36.122 --> 01:04:38.708
You know what?
Better yet, I'll e-mail you the list.


01:04:38.792 --> 01:04:41.545
- What is that?
- Oh, you're not familiar with e-mail?


01:04:41.628 --> 01:04:45.382
E-mail? Of course I heard of that.
Which one are you talking about?


01:04:45.465 --> 01:04:49.636
You got your computer, right?
And you plug that into your phone line,


01:04:49.719 --> 01:04:55.434
and you could send a document to another
computer clear across the country


01:04:55.517 --> 01:04:57.602
in a matter of minutes.


01:04:57.686 --> 01:05:01.398
Who licks the envelope? R2-D2?
I'm lost right now.


01:05:01.481 --> 01:05:04.150
Now I think we're making
a wrong move here.


01:05:04.233 --> 01:05:08.321
I have a publicity campaign designed
strictly for this woman right here.


01:05:08.405 --> 01:05:11.533
You have a publicity campaign? Well,
I mean, we're... The family's all here.


01:05:11.616 --> 01:05:13.367
We would love to hear about it.
What is it?


01:05:13.452 --> 01:05:15.870
Well, I usually like my clients
to start slow.


01:05:15.954 --> 01:05:17.997
Keep it simple. Don't overexpose.


01:05:19.332 --> 01:05:21.250
- Really, Sandy?
- Yes.


01:05:21.334 --> 01:05:23.252
Just gonna spit your chicken on my face?
That's for you.


01:05:24.337 --> 01:05:27.507
Okay. Maybe we'll hold off
on the publicist thing.


01:05:27.591 --> 01:05:28.592
Thank you.


01:05:28.675 --> 01:05:30.343
But then we'll bring in one soon.


01:05:30.427 --> 01:05:32.053
- Okay, boys?
- We'll talk about that.


01:05:32.136 --> 01:05:34.222
Absolutely. I think that's smart.


01:05:34.305 --> 01:05:36.307
All right. I'm gonna go check
on these jeans.


01:05:36.390 --> 01:05:38.309
- Okay?
- Yes, my queen.


01:05:38.392 --> 01:05:39.728
Your queen?


01:05:41.688 --> 01:05:46.150
Sandy, you are the reason
she needs a publicist.


01:05:46.234 --> 01:05:47.611
I'm the reason?


01:05:47.694 --> 01:05:50.489
You know how many calls I got after
Quincy Jones threw you out of his party?


01:05:50.572 --> 01:05:54.451
- Oh... She dared me to do it.
- What are you, 14, Sandy?


01:05:54.534 --> 01:05:56.911
No, I'm not 14. I'm not 14 at all.


01:05:56.995 --> 01:05:58.412
Your job is to protect her.


01:05:58.497 --> 01:06:00.499
I protect her 24/7!


01:06:00.582 --> 01:06:03.167
And how is that?
By screwing up her shot on Arsenio?


01:06:03.251 --> 01:06:04.794
We got the show, didn't we?


01:06:04.878 --> 01:06:06.295
Because I fixed it!


01:06:06.379 --> 01:06:09.423
You fixed it. You did everything.
You invented music.


01:06:09.508 --> 01:06:10.759
What did you do, Sandy?


01:06:10.842 --> 01:06:13.344
Did you file the paperwork for the Grammy
nomination before the deadline?


01:06:13.427 --> 01:06:15.514
Did you squash the story in the Enquirer


01:06:15.597 --> 01:06:18.933
about her corrections officer father
falling asleep during a prison riot?


01:06:19.017 --> 01:06:21.060
Did you send envelopes of cash
to the radio stations


01:06:21.144 --> 01:06:22.436
so they could play her record?


01:06:23.437 --> 01:06:24.939
No, you didn't do that.


01:06:25.023 --> 01:06:26.483
You know how I know
you didn't do it, Sandy?


01:06:26.566 --> 01:06:28.442
Because I did it.
I did all those things.


01:06:28.527 --> 01:06:31.112
And what did you do? Hmm?


01:06:31.195 --> 01:06:35.116
You made sure Gary,
the daredevil trapeze artist,


01:06:35.199 --> 01:06:38.036
was her opening act
at the Universal Amphitheatre.


01:06:39.037 --> 01:06:40.038
Gary is family.


01:06:40.121 --> 01:06:42.791
This dude shattered his pelvis
on an amplifier!


01:06:42.874 --> 01:06:44.501
I was there. I saw.


01:06:44.584 --> 01:06:46.460
There was blood
all over the first three rows!


01:06:46.545 --> 01:06:48.505
- People were vomiting!
- Yeah, all right.


01:06:48.588 --> 01:06:49.798
That doesn't really segue well


01:06:49.881 --> 01:06:52.551
into soulful singer-songwriter now,
does it, Sandy?


01:06:52.634 --> 01:06:55.011
She got 'em back.
She's too good to lose a crowd.


01:06:55.094 --> 01:06:56.513
She's too good for you.


01:06:57.388 --> 01:06:59.098
Sandy, she could have
any manager she wants.


01:06:59.182 --> 01:07:00.266
She wants me!


01:07:00.349 --> 01:07:02.519
And that is what's holding her back.


01:07:04.270 --> 01:07:05.980
Look, Sandy, you did your job.


01:07:06.856 --> 01:07:09.526
You brought her up to the big leagues.


01:07:09.609 --> 01:07:12.070
I'm telling you. Come on!


01:07:12.987 --> 01:07:15.824
But now you're just...
You're out of your depth.


01:07:15.907 --> 01:07:18.284
Don't let your ego get in the way.


01:07:18.993 --> 01:07:23.081
Can you look me in the eye and tell me
you're doing what's best for her?


01:07:27.501 --> 01:07:28.753
- Okay.
- Ah!


01:07:28.837 --> 01:07:31.255
Pants-Off Dance-Off
is officially canceled.


01:07:31.339 --> 01:07:32.716
- Put these bad boys on.
- Okay.


01:07:32.799 --> 01:07:36.803
You got the stain out?
Very nice. Look at you. Look at you.


01:07:36.886 --> 01:07:40.264
Well, I'm beat to shit.
I'm gonna call it.


01:07:40.849 --> 01:07:44.102
You're gonna call it?
All right. I'll walk you out, then.


01:07:44.185 --> 01:07:47.689
Thank you for everything.
Appreciate it all.


01:07:57.115 --> 01:07:59.993
Oh. Oh, yeah. Good night.


01:08:11.630 --> 01:08:13.464
Thanks for scaring the stalker raccoon.


01:08:13.547 --> 01:08:16.760
You don't have to thank me, Courtney.
That's my pleasure.


01:08:16.843 --> 01:08:17.844
Look, Sandy...


01:08:19.553 --> 01:08:21.347
This rock star thing is new to me.


01:08:22.223 --> 01:08:24.558
I'm doing the best I can
to make everybody happy, you know.


01:08:24.643 --> 01:08:28.897
You make the world happy, Courtney.
That's all you need to worry about.


01:08:29.814 --> 01:08:30.899
Thank you, Sandy.


01:08:31.608 --> 01:08:34.402
That's why it's difficult
for me to tell you this.


01:08:34.485 --> 01:08:38.114
But where you are right now
in your career,


01:08:38.197 --> 01:08:41.868
and what it requires of my time, it's...


01:08:44.037 --> 01:08:48.708
I'm being kind of forced here
to make sacrifices that,


01:08:48.792 --> 01:08:52.045
with good conscience,
I don't really wanna make.


01:08:52.128 --> 01:08:53.587
Like what?


01:08:53.672 --> 01:08:57.676
Like my stable of talent.


01:08:57.759 --> 01:09:02.263
I can't give them what I believe
each and every one of them deserves


01:09:02.346 --> 01:09:07.894
if I'm worried about all the
complexities of your day-to-day.


01:09:07.977 --> 01:09:10.146
It's a lot, kid. I'm sorry.


01:09:10.229 --> 01:09:13.316
So what? You don't want
to work together anymore?


01:09:13.399 --> 01:09:17.403
Well, it's just the current situation
isn't fair to you, either.


01:09:17.486 --> 01:09:22.366
I can't commit to you 100%
if I got other things on my mind,


01:09:22.450 --> 01:09:25.119
which unfortunately I do.
The stable.


01:09:25.203 --> 01:09:27.831
Sandy, let's not do this right now.


01:09:29.207 --> 01:09:31.876
Let's take a minute and think it over.


01:09:31.960 --> 01:09:33.878
I don't need a minute.


01:09:33.962 --> 01:09:37.506
I promised your dad
I'd always do what's best for you.


01:09:37.590 --> 01:09:38.925
This is best.


01:09:43.221 --> 01:09:44.388
So that's it?


01:09:46.265 --> 01:09:49.143
You ever need me, just beep.


01:09:51.479 --> 01:09:52.646
Sandy.


01:09:55.942 --> 01:09:56.943
Beep.


01:09:58.737 --> 01:10:00.529
You're gonna be all right, Courtney.


01:10:01.530 --> 01:10:02.949
You're gonna be a legend.


01:10:05.534 --> 01:10:06.995
Brightest star out there.


01:10:31.269 --> 01:10:35.481
Legend has it he stayed in that car
and cried for... six hours?


01:10:40.528 --> 01:10:44.073
Someone called child services 'cause
they thought a little girl was in trouble.


01:10:44.157 --> 01:10:45.158
- Yeah.
- In a car.


01:10:49.829 --> 01:10:51.790
I mean, not that anybody has a good cry,


01:10:51.873 --> 01:10:53.750
but his cry sounded
like some kind of, like,


01:10:53.833 --> 01:10:56.335
lonesome moose.


01:11:02.091 --> 01:11:04.761
Whatever the amount of time was
that he cried,


01:11:04.844 --> 01:11:06.805
he broke his own rules.
He just got too close.


01:11:06.888 --> 01:11:09.182
It was Alfred all over again.


01:11:09.265 --> 01:11:10.516
That was a tough time...


01:11:12.769 --> 01:11:18.441
'cause Sandy not only lost
his most talented client ever,


01:11:18.524 --> 01:11:22.195
but he also lost this person
he had feelings for.


01:11:23.196 --> 01:11:24.948
It must've been
especially painful for Sandy,


01:11:25.031 --> 01:11:27.366
because Courtney Clarke was everywhere.


01:11:30.494 --> 01:11:31.495
Whoo!


01:11:38.920 --> 01:11:41.881
Gary Rodgers, ladies and gentlemen.


01:11:41.964 --> 01:11:45.802
♪ There's something
In the way that you smile ♪


01:11:46.969 --> 01:11:52.266
♪ There's something
In the way that you talk to me ♪


01:11:52.350 --> 01:11:57.355
♪ The way that you look at me
Boy, I can't see anything... ♪


01:11:57.438 --> 01:11:59.482
Yo, man, your girl blew up.
She the shit now.


01:11:59.565 --> 01:12:01.609
- Congratulations, Sandy.
- Yeah.


01:12:01.692 --> 01:12:03.777
Yeah, she's doing great. Uh...


01:12:03.862 --> 01:12:06.114
We're not working together
anymore, though.


01:12:07.198 --> 01:12:09.783
Oh. Now that makes sense.


01:12:09.868 --> 01:12:11.160
Later, dawg.


01:12:11.244 --> 01:12:13.496
Yeah. That makes sense.


01:12:14.330 --> 01:12:16.875
It makes sense if I kill you, Arsenio.


01:12:18.001 --> 01:12:19.210
That would make sense.


01:12:19.293 --> 01:12:22.630
♪ I know it is destiny ♪


01:12:26.300 --> 01:12:29.803
♪ Hot summer nights, lovers ♪


01:12:29.888 --> 01:12:31.305
Get out of town with that.


01:12:31.389 --> 01:12:34.058
♪ Samba dancing with
Fire in their eyes burning ♪


01:12:34.142 --> 01:12:35.184
Come on.


01:12:35.894 --> 01:12:39.063
♪ Hearts on full with desire ♪


01:12:39.147 --> 01:12:42.525
♪ Wanting you, wanting me ♪


01:12:42.608 --> 01:12:47.613
♪ Gonna make you wanna fall in love
Love, love, love ♪


01:12:48.697 --> 01:12:51.659
♪ Yeah, I think I'm gonna fall in love ♪


01:12:52.368 --> 01:12:55.663
Oh, jeez, you're going for this?
Give me a break here.


01:12:55.746 --> 01:12:59.500
♪ Samba dancing with
Fire in their eyes burning ♪


01:12:59.583 --> 01:13:03.546
♪ Hearts on full with desire... ♪


01:13:03.629 --> 01:13:05.006
All right. That's enough.


01:13:06.049 --> 01:13:07.175
Come on, already.


01:13:50.468 --> 01:13:51.885
What have we got here?


01:13:54.931 --> 01:13:57.391
Sandy!


01:13:57.475 --> 01:13:59.518
I was scared you wouldn't come.


01:14:01.062 --> 01:14:04.398
Hey. Where's Peter? Is he doing PT?


01:14:04.482 --> 01:14:07.651
Sandy, why don't you
take off your shoes?


01:14:07.735 --> 01:14:10.238
Take off my... Oh, for your rug?


01:14:10.321 --> 01:14:12.240
You know, my shoes are actually cleaner


01:14:12.323 --> 01:14:14.867
than my socks, but...


01:14:14.951 --> 01:14:16.369
And here we are.


01:14:17.996 --> 01:14:19.956
- Hey, hey.
- And here's your throne.


01:14:20.039 --> 01:14:22.083
Why don't you sit down, Sandy?


01:14:22.166 --> 01:14:24.252
- Hey.
- What would you like to drink?


01:14:24.335 --> 01:14:26.462
You know, I got a bit of a sour stomach.


01:14:26.545 --> 01:14:30.633
If you got Dr. Brown's black cherry
diet, that would be perfect.


01:14:32.593 --> 01:14:35.638
Or a big glass of whiskey.
Either way is...


01:14:45.398 --> 01:14:46.399
Oh, look.


01:14:46.983 --> 01:14:48.734
Ah.


01:14:52.488 --> 01:14:56.700
Did you ever see
that naughty little movie, 9½ Weeks?


01:14:56.784 --> 01:14:58.119
No, I didn't.


01:14:58.202 --> 01:15:01.414
I saw Problem Child, though.
That kid was hysterical.


01:15:03.582 --> 01:15:07.586
Well, not as funny as that.
Look at you.


01:15:08.421 --> 01:15:11.465
- Peter's been sick for a long time.
- Yeah.


01:15:12.466 --> 01:15:14.927
And a woman yearns for a man's touch.


01:15:15.636 --> 01:15:17.138
Hey, no, that's natural.


01:15:17.221 --> 01:15:19.098
Are you a man, Sandy?


01:15:20.183 --> 01:15:21.975
I don't know. I...


01:15:22.060 --> 01:15:24.645
I was bar mitzvahed,
but that was a long time ago.


01:15:27.565 --> 01:15:29.567
- You know what I love about you?
- Yeah?


01:15:29.650 --> 01:15:31.860
Your voice.


01:15:31.944 --> 01:15:34.113
Come on. I've got a surprise.


01:15:35.448 --> 01:15:36.574
- Come along.
- Hey, what's this?


01:15:36.657 --> 01:15:38.951
- Just sit here. Now, sit.
- Oh! Oh, yeah.


01:15:39.035 --> 01:15:41.620
Aye, aye, aye! Yeah!


01:15:41.704 --> 01:15:43.497
Touch me, Sandy. Touch me.


01:15:43.581 --> 01:15:46.584
Well, I... I was just walking
on the carpet in my socks.


01:15:46.667 --> 01:15:51.630
- I don't wanna zap you.
- Oh. You can zap me. Just zap me.


01:15:55.343 --> 01:15:57.095
Cindy!


01:16:06.812 --> 01:16:11.024
Don't worry about Peter.
He only wants my happiness.


01:16:11.109 --> 01:16:12.360
Yeah.


01:16:18.907 --> 01:16:21.410
I can't do it. I can't.


01:16:21.494 --> 01:16:23.954
- I'd feel better if we...
- Don't, Sandy, please.


01:16:24.038 --> 01:16:26.540
- Don't leave. Stay here.
- Oh...


01:16:26.624 --> 01:16:28.459
We... we could put a blanket
over his head.


01:16:29.293 --> 01:16:33.256
That's... that's actually a thought.


01:16:33.339 --> 01:16:36.008
No. He says no. He said... I'm sorry.


01:16:36.092 --> 01:16:39.220
I consider Peter a friend,


01:16:39.303 --> 01:16:43.141
whether he's alive or dead
or in a vegetative state.


01:16:43.224 --> 01:16:45.601
Thanks for the offer, okay?


01:16:46.810 --> 01:16:50.063
I got the shock! I knew I... The socks.


01:16:57.405 --> 01:16:58.406
Pervert.


01:17:03.744 --> 01:17:04.870
- Cindy!
- Cindy!


01:17:04.953 --> 01:17:06.247
Madonna!


01:17:06.330 --> 01:17:07.415
Melissa!


01:17:08.291 --> 01:17:10.834
Wrapping up the CDs.


01:17:10.918 --> 01:17:13.045
Doing too good a job. I feel that...


01:17:14.505 --> 01:17:18.091
Just... a little bit overzealous
with the wrapping is my feeling.


01:17:18.176 --> 01:17:21.470
What is the security on this thing?


01:17:21.554 --> 01:17:22.846
It's a $12 item.


01:17:22.930 --> 01:17:24.848
They got it wrapped up
like the Hope Diamond.


01:17:25.974 --> 01:17:27.768
It's impossible
that they have cellophane...


01:17:27.851 --> 01:17:32.022
What are you doing? You look gloomy.
Reiser's killing out there. Come on.


01:17:32.105 --> 01:17:34.775
You're like a monkey with a coconut.
You're just looking at it...


01:17:34.858 --> 01:17:37.653
He's killing the jokes that I wrote.
It should be me up there killing it.


01:17:37.736 --> 01:17:41.407
Next year, it will be.
CBS sees your jokes work now.


01:17:41.490 --> 01:17:44.327
Next year, you'll be telling those
jokes, 'cause you wrote 'em.


01:17:48.080 --> 01:17:51.209
You want me to do the jokes
he's telling right now


01:17:51.292 --> 01:17:52.293
on next year's Grammys?


01:17:52.376 --> 01:17:54.170
But you do 'em in your voice.


01:17:54.253 --> 01:17:56.672
But the punch lines are the same.
People have heard them already.


01:17:56.755 --> 01:17:58.299
You do new punch lines.


01:17:58.382 --> 01:18:00.509
So then they're new...
They're new jokes.


01:18:00.593 --> 01:18:02.761
No, but you're doing 'em in your voice.


01:18:02.845 --> 01:18:04.222
I wanna strangle you.


01:18:04.305 --> 01:18:05.806
- Don't say "your voice" again.
- What are you...


01:18:05.889 --> 01:18:07.558
I'm gonna kill you
if you say "in my voice."


01:18:07.641 --> 01:18:09.768
- Would you stop? I can't ever...
- Sandy?


01:18:12.355 --> 01:18:13.356
Courtney.


01:18:14.607 --> 01:18:16.359
Look at you!


01:18:16.442 --> 01:18:19.945
- Hey! Hey.
- Hey! Oh.


01:18:21.739 --> 01:18:25.618
You, uh, remember my, uh,
client Paul Reiser?


01:18:26.619 --> 01:18:28.746
- Kevin Connors.
- Kevin!


01:18:29.455 --> 01:18:31.540
They should have had you host this show.


01:18:31.624 --> 01:18:35.669
Paul Reiser is usually funny,
but his jokes tonight are just corny.


01:18:37.380 --> 01:18:39.673
- You still doing Atkins? I see.
- Atkins.


01:18:39.757 --> 01:18:41.467
- You look great!
- Thank you. Well, my God.


01:18:41.550 --> 01:18:43.135
- I look good? Look at you.
- You look so good!


01:18:43.219 --> 01:18:45.929
I have been following you.
You are doing so well.


01:18:46.013 --> 01:18:49.600
The Grammy tonight. Did I tell you
when that was gonna happen, huh?


01:18:49.683 --> 01:18:51.227
You deserve it all. You really do.


01:18:51.310 --> 01:18:54.605
You deserve it, too.
I wouldn't be here without you.


01:18:54.688 --> 01:18:57.775
Are you kidding me?
You cannot stop a shooting star.


01:18:57.858 --> 01:18:59.735
- Aw.
- Our scientists have proven this.


01:19:00.361 --> 01:19:02.321
You are unbelievable, Sandy.


01:19:02.405 --> 01:19:04.407
How's Bling? Where is he?


01:19:04.490 --> 01:19:07.660
Yeah, he's my label guy.
He's not my guy-guy anymore.


01:19:07.743 --> 01:19:11.079
- Well, I'm so sorry. That's...
- Don't be.


01:19:11.163 --> 01:19:12.998
Things happen for a reason.


01:19:13.081 --> 01:19:14.625
I scored us each a goodie bag, my sweet.


01:19:14.708 --> 01:19:16.960
- Hi, cuteness.
- Can I keep your PlayStation?


01:19:17.044 --> 01:19:18.296
Yes.


01:19:18.379 --> 01:19:24.009
Guys, this is my new boyfriend, Ra...
Say it for me, babe.


01:19:24.092 --> 01:19:25.511
Ramiro Alejandro.


01:19:25.594 --> 01:19:29.307
- Sandy Wexler.
- Nice to meet you, Ramir...


01:19:29.390 --> 01:19:31.183
- Ramiro Alejandro.
- I know.


01:19:31.267 --> 01:19:34.395
Oh, is this the old Make-A-Wish guy
you were telling me about?


01:19:34.478 --> 01:19:37.105
No. No, we used to work together.


01:19:37.189 --> 01:19:40.150
Hey, you wanna come to Clive Davis'
after-party? You could ride with us.


01:19:40.233 --> 01:19:42.069
I, uh, would love to.


01:19:42.152 --> 01:19:44.405
- I, uh, have to go somewhere.
- Aw.


01:19:44.488 --> 01:19:47.491
A client of mine... Amy Baskin.
You... you remember Amy.


01:19:47.575 --> 01:19:48.576
Yeah!


01:19:48.659 --> 01:19:52.913
Yes, well, she got the lead in "Sound
of Music" at the Pasadena Playhouse.


01:19:52.996 --> 01:19:56.917
- She'll be Partygoer Number One.
- Yeah, that's the lead.


01:19:57.000 --> 01:19:59.545
It is. She's...
She's the lead partygoer.


01:19:59.628 --> 01:20:02.798
Let's get together real soon, Sandy.
Promise me.


01:20:02.881 --> 01:20:05.759
- I promise. You promise me this.
- Of course. What?


01:20:05.843 --> 01:20:07.177
- After Clive's party...
- Mmm-hmm.


01:20:07.260 --> 01:20:09.638
- ...you put on the ugly duckling hat...
- Oh, gosh.


01:20:09.722 --> 01:20:11.682
...and you remind yourself
where you came from.


01:20:11.765 --> 01:20:13.058
Not on this hair.


01:20:13.141 --> 01:20:15.143
- Like we... Nope, not on your hair.
- Courtney...


01:20:15.227 --> 01:20:16.729
- You promise?
- ...we have to go.


01:20:16.812 --> 01:20:18.522
- I promise. Okay.
- I gotta see you. Okay.


01:20:18.606 --> 01:20:20.399
Good to see you, babe.


01:20:20.483 --> 01:20:23.944
Nice meeting you, Sammy!
Hope they find a cure for you, buddy.


01:20:24.027 --> 01:20:25.821
Buddy, move. Move!


01:20:25.904 --> 01:20:27.656
- Get out the way!
- Which way are you moving?


01:20:27.740 --> 01:20:28.866
- Okay, go!
- Sandy, move! Sandy!


01:20:28.949 --> 01:20:30.743
That was another tough
goodbye for Sandy.


01:20:30.826 --> 01:20:34.121
He... he didn't even know if he would
ever see or talk to Courtney again.


01:20:34.204 --> 01:20:35.664
Of course he kept himself busy.


01:20:35.748 --> 01:20:37.249
He actually signed someone


01:20:37.333 --> 01:20:40.210
who was involved in the biggest form
of entertainment in the '90s.


01:20:40.293 --> 01:20:41.795
Wrestling. Professional wrestling.


01:20:45.090 --> 01:20:47.676
Yeah!


01:20:56.935 --> 01:20:57.936
Yeah!


01:21:07.446 --> 01:21:12.284
Go to sleep, baby!
It's night-night time!


01:21:23.295 --> 01:21:25.005
- You're the man, Bedtime.
- Isn't he?


01:21:25.088 --> 01:21:26.757
Oh, I know you're gonna
take the title on Sunday.


01:21:26.840 --> 01:21:29.885
I'm gonna make 'em go night-night.


01:21:30.969 --> 01:21:33.764
- Thank you.
- I'm gonna lose.


01:21:33.847 --> 01:21:35.724
You don't know that. Hang on, please.


01:21:35.808 --> 01:21:38.727
Yeah, I do know that. I got the script.


01:21:38.811 --> 01:21:42.440
Tsunami sits on my face until I tap out.
I'm never gonna be the champ.


01:21:42.523 --> 01:21:43.691
Okay, look.


01:21:43.774 --> 01:21:47.820
The good thing is, you're gonna have
a grown man sit on your face,


01:21:47.903 --> 01:21:51.156
and the entire world is gonna
be watching. That's a positive.


01:21:51.239 --> 01:21:53.325
- That's not a positive.
- It's a positive because it's...


01:21:53.409 --> 01:21:54.702
- The fame factor.
- What?


01:21:54.785 --> 01:21:57.955
Hey, Bedtime. Will you rock me like a baby
while my brother Dicky gets a picture?


01:21:58.038 --> 01:21:59.957
- What are you, six?
- Yeah, of course he will.


01:22:00.040 --> 01:22:02.167
- Of course he will do it.
- Do you see the size of this guy?


01:22:02.250 --> 01:22:03.293
Just get on it.


01:22:03.376 --> 01:22:07.297
Oh. Hang on, guys.
My cellular device is ringing.


01:22:08.048 --> 01:22:10.383
And I hit this, and I pull this.


01:22:11.218 --> 01:22:12.344
Wexler Artists.


01:22:12.428 --> 01:22:14.847
Mr. Wexler, it is
Chippy from Dan Tana's.


01:22:14.930 --> 01:22:19.685
Chippy! Hey! How's it going?
How was your vacation to Cincinnati?


01:22:19.768 --> 01:22:22.395
It was, uh, not a vacation.
My mother died.


01:22:22.480 --> 01:22:24.022
I went to Cincinnati for the funeral.


01:22:24.106 --> 01:22:26.358
Oh, yeah. That's right.
How's your mother?


01:22:27.985 --> 01:22:29.194
What are you calling for?


01:22:29.277 --> 01:22:32.990
We have a delicate situation with a client
of yours who has had too much to drink.


01:22:33.073 --> 01:22:35.826
And unfortunately,
there are very many paparazzi out front.


01:22:37.035 --> 01:22:39.204
Oh, boy. Was it Gary or Kevin?


01:22:44.376 --> 01:22:46.336
Yeah, I chased him
for six or seven blocks.


01:22:46.419 --> 01:22:50.173
Just come on. Get a life, guys. Jeez.


01:22:56.429 --> 01:22:58.223
- Bring me to the package.
- This way.


01:23:07.816 --> 01:23:09.026
Courtney?


01:23:10.360 --> 01:23:13.446
What the... What's going on, kiddo?


01:23:14.031 --> 01:23:16.324
Sandy! They found you!


01:23:16.408 --> 01:23:17.868
Yeah, they found me.


01:23:17.951 --> 01:23:21.288
You just stay put, okay?
You stay right there.


01:23:26.084 --> 01:23:28.462
Aw, Sandy to the rescue.


01:23:29.379 --> 01:23:32.675
No one can find out about this.
You understand me, Chippy? Not even you.


01:23:33.717 --> 01:23:34.885
Okay, Sandy.


01:23:36.303 --> 01:23:37.763
- Okay.
- Sandy!


01:23:39.807 --> 01:23:42.810
What? She'll suffocate?
Is that what you're saying?


01:23:42.893 --> 01:23:45.353
Courtney! Courtney! Courtney!


01:23:45.437 --> 01:23:47.314
Go jump in a lake, fellas!


01:23:53.070 --> 01:23:57.741
Ah! No, no, no, no! Oh, come on!
Oh, please, please, please.


01:23:58.951 --> 01:24:01.494
Keep your voices down. Let her sleep.


01:24:03.121 --> 01:24:06.625
That's right. Just sleep. Sleep, sleep.


01:24:07.209 --> 01:24:09.545
Let me get this up for you.


01:24:10.462 --> 01:24:13.131
And you... you're breathing.


01:24:13.882 --> 01:24:15.050
Are you breathing?


01:24:15.759 --> 01:24:17.761
Yeah, there it is. Okay.


01:24:17.845 --> 01:24:18.929
You'll be all right.


01:24:21.056 --> 01:24:24.893
I'm telling you, he's the best
ventriloquist in the business. He...


01:24:24.977 --> 01:24:26.436
You don't see him talking?


01:24:26.519 --> 01:24:31.441
No, you see his lips move slightly,
but that's not the important thing.


01:24:31.524 --> 01:24:34.069
The important thing
is what the guy is saying.


01:24:34.152 --> 01:24:37.197
No one looks at the lips
if they're laughing, then...


01:24:37.280 --> 01:24:38.949
No, kids love him.


01:24:39.032 --> 01:24:42.786
That's why I'm bringing it up
to you. The kids will love this guy.


01:24:42.870 --> 01:24:46.373
He's got curly hair,
and... and he's got the mustache.


01:24:46.456 --> 01:24:47.457
I'm sorry.


01:24:47.540 --> 01:24:50.502
- Linda, I'm... I'm just asking if you...
- Do you want some breakfast?


01:24:50.586 --> 01:24:52.504
- Sandy...
- If you could just


01:24:52.588 --> 01:24:54.547
put a good word in for me. That's it.


01:24:54.632 --> 01:24:56.717
Maybe put his headshot on his desk.


01:24:56.800 --> 01:24:59.136
- I really wish I could, Sandy.
- Hey, just meat, right?


01:24:59.219 --> 01:25:01.554
Oh, yeah. Hold on. Just meat.


01:25:02.598 --> 01:25:03.766
Just meet with him.


01:25:04.474 --> 01:25:06.852
That's all I'm asking you to do.
Just meet with him.


01:25:06.935 --> 01:25:08.103
All right, Sandy.


01:25:08.186 --> 01:25:11.564
Thank you, Linda! Thank you!


01:25:11.649 --> 01:25:13.525
Happy birthday on Wednesday.


01:25:13.609 --> 01:25:15.903
- How did you know that?
- Yeah, 'cause I know.


01:25:15.986 --> 01:25:18.238
'Cause I know. I know everything.


01:25:20.073 --> 01:25:22.618
How good is this? Phenomenal.


01:25:22.701 --> 01:25:24.662
No one knows
how to cook health food like...


01:25:24.745 --> 01:25:27.205
You're fantastic. You can do it all.


01:25:27.915 --> 01:25:31.293
I owe you for last night.
I'm embarrassed.


01:25:31.960 --> 01:25:34.462
Hey, everybody gets zonked
once in a while.


01:25:34.546 --> 01:25:36.924
The question is, why are we doing it?


01:25:38.175 --> 01:25:39.593
I don't know. I...


01:25:40.135 --> 01:25:41.594
I just broke up with Billy.


01:25:41.679 --> 01:25:45.432
Billy? Who's Billy?
What happened to the Marc Anthony fella?


01:25:45.515 --> 01:25:47.059
Marc Anthony? Come on, Sandy.


01:25:47.142 --> 01:25:49.687
Pick up a People magazine
every once in a while.


01:25:49.770 --> 01:25:51.855
That was three boyfriends ago.


01:25:51.939 --> 01:25:55.525
Oh, hey, I gotta start writing
some of these names down.


01:25:55.608 --> 01:25:58.737
I'm getting lost.
I'm joking around with you.


01:25:58.821 --> 01:26:01.239
What you're doing's perfectly natural.


01:26:01.323 --> 01:26:03.742
Anyone in your position
would be doing the same.


01:26:03.826 --> 01:26:05.160
Look, Liza did it.


01:26:05.869 --> 01:26:08.956
Elizabeth Taylor did it.
Sherwood Schwartz did it.


01:26:09.039 --> 01:26:11.583
Just my life.


01:26:12.710 --> 01:26:14.419
It feels out of control.


01:26:14.502 --> 01:26:18.882
I can't connect with anybody.
I don't... I just don't feel safe.


01:26:18.966 --> 01:26:20.926
I can't even go ten feet


01:26:21.009 --> 01:26:25.806
without the paparazzi following me,
taking pictures of me, spying on me.


01:26:25.889 --> 01:26:27.390
I don't even want to
leave my house anymore.


01:26:27.474 --> 01:26:29.101
What? You gotta leave your house.


01:26:29.184 --> 01:26:32.062
Even Michael Jackson
leaves his house once in a while.


01:26:32.813 --> 01:26:33.647
How?


01:26:33.731 --> 01:26:36.734
He just don't look like Michael Jackson.


01:26:40.570 --> 01:26:42.655
Excuse me, sir.
You know what time it is?


01:26:45.617 --> 01:26:47.160
Can you do me a favor?


01:26:47.244 --> 01:26:50.789
Courtney Clarke was just in there.
Uh, could you find out where she went?


01:26:50.873 --> 01:26:53.625
This is...
Somebody just got their life back!


01:26:53.709 --> 01:26:56.378
...Why do you own this stuff?


01:26:56.461 --> 01:26:58.839
Why? Those are my workout clothes.


01:26:58.922 --> 01:27:00.799
You work out?


01:27:00.883 --> 01:27:04.928
Suzanne Somers personally gave me
one of the very first ThighMasters.


01:27:05.012 --> 01:27:06.263
I use it as much as I can.


01:27:06.346 --> 01:27:08.015
This conversation is over.


01:27:08.098 --> 01:27:10.392
What? It's for firm thighs and buttocks.


01:27:10.475 --> 01:27:12.936
- Sandy, please stop talking.
- All right.


01:27:13.686 --> 01:27:14.772
What we gonna do today?


01:27:14.855 --> 01:27:17.733
What we gonna do today?
Anything you want, kiddo.


01:27:17.816 --> 01:27:20.861
- Okay, lead the way, ThighMaster.
- Hey! Now, wait a minute.


01:27:20.944 --> 01:27:23.864
- By the way, the dogs are good for cardio.
- Oh.


01:27:24.907 --> 01:27:25.908
What does that mean?


01:27:25.991 --> 01:27:27.159
You'll see.


01:27:27.242 --> 01:27:29.995
- Go! Run! Run! Run!
- Okay! Okay!


01:27:31.872 --> 01:27:33.581
Well, here comes the test.


01:27:34.792 --> 01:27:37.585
Look at that. Look at that. Huh?


01:27:37.669 --> 01:27:39.254
...Wow.


01:27:40.798 --> 01:27:42.215
Why am I golfing?


01:27:42.299 --> 01:27:44.134
Golfing is very relaxing.


01:27:44.217 --> 01:27:47.512
You don't have to think
about nothing but smacking that ball.


01:27:47.595 --> 01:27:49.306
Have you ever played before?


01:27:49.389 --> 01:27:52.225
- No.
- No? It's quite easy.


01:27:52.309 --> 01:27:55.687
I'll take out the big stick
'cause it's fun to hit 'em far.


01:27:55.771 --> 01:27:59.316
It's always good to warm up a little bit.
Ow! Okay.


01:27:59.399 --> 01:28:02.235
I got actually a little problem
in the back.


01:28:02.319 --> 01:28:04.696
- You okay?
- Yeah. Just give me one sec.


01:28:04.780 --> 01:28:05.781
God damn it.


01:28:05.864 --> 01:28:07.699
- Should I call for help?
- No, I'll be all right.


01:28:07.783 --> 01:28:09.993
Just give me one sec.
I just gotta stretch.


01:28:11.787 --> 01:28:14.915
All right. Just give me one more sec.
I do need help.


01:28:22.089 --> 01:28:23.631
You need to go to the bathroom?


01:28:23.715 --> 01:28:26.259
No, I'm just... I'm getting it lined up.


01:28:27.385 --> 01:28:30.931
Let's just say goodbye
to all our troubles, okay?


01:28:31.014 --> 01:28:32.015
Okay.


01:28:32.099 --> 01:28:35.102
If you got any problems, put 'em
into the ball and send them away.


01:28:37.604 --> 01:28:40.357
Is it supposed to curve
off to the right like that?


01:28:40.440 --> 01:28:42.609
Yeah, I was playing a dogleg right.


01:28:42.692 --> 01:28:44.402
- A dogleg?
- Right.


01:28:44.486 --> 01:28:47.489
You gotta bend it around the trees,
and that's what I was going for.


01:28:47.572 --> 01:28:49.657
- Can I try it?
- You wanna try? Okay.


01:28:49.741 --> 01:28:51.701
I was gonna show you
a little more, but okay.


01:28:51.784 --> 01:28:53.370
- Okay.
- So let me...


01:28:53.453 --> 01:28:55.163
You know, maybe you should
tee it up for yourself.


01:28:55.247 --> 01:28:56.539
Tee it up. Here.


01:28:56.623 --> 01:28:59.001
- You tee it up, and you say goodbye.
- Right here.


01:28:59.084 --> 01:29:00.085
Okay.


01:29:00.168 --> 01:29:02.045
And just have a good time
and don't worry about where it goes.


01:29:02.129 --> 01:29:03.839
- Let's see.
- Okay.


01:29:08.343 --> 01:29:11.179
Am I being hustled right now?
What was that?


01:29:11.263 --> 01:29:15.350
I swear I didn't play every day growing up
with my Uncle Davey who's a golf pro.


01:29:15.433 --> 01:29:17.227
Oh, well...


01:29:17.310 --> 01:29:19.855
Does this guy need a manager because...


01:29:19.938 --> 01:29:21.773
- Come over here.
- What are we doing?


01:29:21.857 --> 01:29:23.108
We gotta work on that slice leg.


01:29:23.191 --> 01:29:24.692
- Oh, my God.
- Here you go. Here you go.


01:29:24.776 --> 01:29:26.904
- This is your day. I don't want to...
- No. No, no, no. You got it?


01:29:26.987 --> 01:29:29.322
- You're okay with it?
- Oh, it's my day now. Come on.


01:29:29.406 --> 01:29:30.615
- In the hips.
- In the hips.


01:29:30.698 --> 01:29:31.699
Here we go.


01:29:31.783 --> 01:29:34.494
Oh! All right! Hold on now.


01:29:35.120 --> 01:29:37.705
Huh? I beg your pardon?


01:29:37.789 --> 01:29:38.790
Tell me. Tell me.


01:29:38.874 --> 01:29:40.000
A company called Pixar...


01:29:40.083 --> 01:29:41.334
- Pixar?
- ...wants me to do a voice


01:29:41.418 --> 01:29:43.545
in some animated movie
about a bunch of toys.


01:29:43.628 --> 01:29:45.005
Cartoons are dead.


01:29:45.088 --> 01:29:46.589
Tell 'em pass.


01:29:46.673 --> 01:29:49.176
- Okay. Sandy knows best.
- I mean, come on. I do know best.


01:29:49.259 --> 01:29:53.555
The lady at Chili's said they'll keep it
open till 10:30 for us, so that's good.


01:29:53.638 --> 01:29:54.973
How you feeling anyway?


01:29:55.057 --> 01:29:56.141
As good as anybody can feel


01:29:56.224 --> 01:29:58.393
knowing they're about to get
their face sat on by that guy.


01:29:59.352 --> 01:30:00.562
Damn, that's a big ass!


01:30:00.645 --> 01:30:02.272
- That's right...
- Get off me!


01:30:02.355 --> 01:30:05.442
Listen. Will you just trust me?
This is a good night for you.


01:30:05.525 --> 01:30:06.651
Trust you? It's humiliating.


01:30:06.734 --> 01:30:09.446
My kids are out there, man!
My wife might not ever kiss me again!


01:30:09.529 --> 01:30:12.490
Randy Savage had to get whooped 24 times


01:30:12.574 --> 01:30:15.868
before he finally pinned Ted DiBiase
to win the belt, man!


01:30:15.953 --> 01:30:18.455
How does your platinum-selling ass
know about wrestling history?


01:30:18.538 --> 01:30:21.708
I'm from Alaska.
It was either watch wrestling or fish.


01:30:21.791 --> 01:30:23.376
Is that adorable?


01:30:23.460 --> 01:30:26.379
Will you just take it all in
and promise me you'll have fun?


01:30:26.463 --> 01:30:28.923
This is a big night for you.
Look at me.


01:30:29.007 --> 01:30:31.593
Man, how does your goofy ass
have me feeling good right now?


01:30:31.676 --> 01:30:32.677
That's impossible!


01:30:32.760 --> 01:30:35.472
Because you know I love ya
and I'm your family.


01:30:35.555 --> 01:30:37.224
All right, good luck.


01:30:37.307 --> 01:30:38.641
Get out there!


01:30:43.271 --> 01:30:44.647
Yeah! Come on!


01:30:53.823 --> 01:30:55.908
Fight!


01:30:59.204 --> 01:31:00.288
Okay.


01:31:16.638 --> 01:31:17.847
No!


01:31:24.771 --> 01:31:26.064
Break, break, break, break!


01:31:26.898 --> 01:31:29.817
Hey, what are you doing?
Stick to the script.


01:31:29.901 --> 01:31:31.736
I'm sorry, Tsunami.
You're gonna have to earn this one.


01:31:31.819 --> 01:31:33.030
What? Hey...


01:31:37.325 --> 01:31:39.952
This is bullshit.
I'm supposed to win.


01:31:40.037 --> 01:31:42.622
This happening?
Huh, this is happening?


01:31:42.705 --> 01:31:43.790
Well, bring it on!


01:31:49.837 --> 01:31:51.839
Okay, get back there, champ!


01:31:54.592 --> 01:31:56.636
There it is. Now it's getting real.


01:32:00.807 --> 01:32:02.016
Thank you very much!


01:32:06.563 --> 01:32:07.439
What is this?


01:32:15.197 --> 01:32:17.532
No, you're not! What's going on here?


01:32:26.833 --> 01:32:27.917
Say it!


01:32:28.000 --> 01:32:30.212
It's time to go night-night!


01:32:50.440 --> 01:32:53.151
- I got the belt! I'm the champ!
- You the man! You the man!


01:32:53.235 --> 01:32:56.028
- Sandy! How?
- What do you... Huh?


01:32:56.613 --> 01:33:01.784
The referee is a client, and
Wexler Artists look out for each other.


01:33:01.868 --> 01:33:04.078
Oh, man!
Those guys are gonna fire his ass!


01:33:04.162 --> 01:33:05.705
Of course they are,


01:33:05.788 --> 01:33:09.667
but I already got him a job as a referee
for the Harlem Globetrotters.


01:33:09.751 --> 01:33:12.086
- I know. I understand.
- You're never going to work again!


01:33:12.170 --> 01:33:14.547
What do you say, champ? Proud of ya.


01:33:15.465 --> 01:33:18.135
Oh! I'm so happy, Sandy!


01:33:18.218 --> 01:33:21.721
I love you. This is your moment.
This is all you.


01:33:21.804 --> 01:33:24.432
I'm just so happy for you
and your wife and your kids.


01:33:24.516 --> 01:33:25.767
Okay? That's all I want.


01:33:25.850 --> 01:33:28.186
- I love you! I love you!
- You deserve everything!


01:33:28.270 --> 01:33:30.980
- Courtney, get in here!
- You deserve everything!


01:33:31.063 --> 01:33:32.774
Uh, we do have to go to Chili's, though.


01:33:32.857 --> 01:33:35.527
I told the lady we'd be there
by 10:30, so let's get going.


01:33:35.610 --> 01:33:38.112
- Why are you talking about Chili's now?
- I just don't wanna...


01:33:38.196 --> 01:33:41.324
I don't want her to screw us
for the next time, you know. Let's go.


01:33:55.338 --> 01:33:57.965
Eat up those baby backs, guys.


01:33:59.884 --> 01:34:04.806
How do you take care of everybody
and never worry about yourself?


01:34:06.015 --> 01:34:07.767
How do you become Sandy?


01:34:07.850 --> 01:34:09.394
Oh, well, listen.


01:34:09.477 --> 01:34:13.064
How do you get to Carnegie Hall?
Practice, practice, practice.


01:34:13.147 --> 01:34:14.774
- Hmm.
- Huh?


01:34:17.610 --> 01:34:19.779
I wish I could stay here.


01:34:19.862 --> 01:34:22.657
This is the best day I've had in years.


01:34:24.326 --> 01:34:27.119
Listen, you can stay
as long as you want.


01:34:28.205 --> 01:34:30.373
I'm supposed to go to New York tomorrow


01:34:30.457 --> 01:34:33.418
and shoot this VH1 thing
with Lenny Kravitz.


01:34:34.168 --> 01:34:35.169
Yeah?


01:34:36.463 --> 01:34:37.755
That's a good thing.


01:34:38.840 --> 01:34:39.841
Is it?


01:34:41.384 --> 01:34:42.719
Then why don't I wanna go?


01:34:48.308 --> 01:34:49.767
Tell me I don't have to go, Sandy.


01:34:51.728 --> 01:34:53.355
No, no, no.


01:34:54.772 --> 01:34:55.898
Why won't you?


01:34:57.400 --> 01:34:59.902
'Cause that's not my job anymore.


01:35:01.070 --> 01:35:02.447
Okay.


01:35:03.281 --> 01:35:04.782
What do you want me to do?


01:35:07.577 --> 01:35:12.457
What I want you to do
is concentrate on your career.


01:35:12.540 --> 01:35:14.208
Music comes first.


01:35:15.418 --> 01:35:17.003
Go to New York.


01:35:21.508 --> 01:35:24.135
- You know what?
- What?


01:35:25.970 --> 01:35:27.555
You're a jerk.


01:35:37.357 --> 01:35:39.150
Oh, God, yes!


01:35:40.360 --> 01:35:41.819
What was that?


01:35:42.695 --> 01:35:45.031
- Firuz!
- Oh, all right, then.


01:35:45.114 --> 01:35:46.824
I'll go take a walk or something.


01:35:47.534 --> 01:35:49.661
Have the best night of your life, Sandy.


01:35:50.787 --> 01:35:52.246
I'm trying.


01:35:54.832 --> 01:35:57.001
Ultimately, I have to move.


01:36:34.664 --> 01:36:37.834
The day was perfect,
the night was better.


01:36:37.917 --> 01:36:40.420
Thank you. I'm off to New York.


01:36:40.503 --> 01:36:42.339
Sandy knows best.


01:36:42.422 --> 01:36:43.673
Love, Court.


01:36:51.305 --> 01:36:54.100
- Pick that up!
- Shut up, Firuz!


01:36:57.311 --> 01:36:58.980
Just shut up.


01:36:59.063 --> 01:37:00.732
Success can be really lonely.


01:37:00.815 --> 01:37:03.443
That's why you kinda long
for someone to share it with.


01:37:03.526 --> 01:37:06.028
So a week later,
her and Lenny Kravitz moved in together.


01:37:06.112 --> 01:37:08.698
And then two weeks later after that,
moved out.


01:37:08.781 --> 01:37:10.116
And she moved on to Johnny Depp.


01:37:10.199 --> 01:37:11.409
- Chris Cornell.
- George Clooney.


01:37:11.493 --> 01:37:13.327
- Ziggy Marley.
- Pauly Shore.


01:37:13.411 --> 01:37:15.037
I went out with her?


01:37:15.121 --> 01:37:17.415
Man, Sandy was messed up.


01:37:18.750 --> 01:37:20.418
Sir, are you committing suicide?


01:37:20.502 --> 01:37:22.504
'Cause I don't think
I'm allowed to film that!


01:37:22.587 --> 01:37:24.213
No, I'm not!


01:37:24.296 --> 01:37:26.466
I'm fine, thank you very much!


01:37:26.549 --> 01:37:30.302
She can date whoever she wants to date!
That's her thing!


01:37:30.387 --> 01:37:32.930
- He's talking to me.
- He's talking to you?


01:37:39.145 --> 01:37:43.232
Sandy, that pool looks far away.
How long until my skin starts burning?


01:37:43.315 --> 01:37:49.155
I think the safety advisor
said four seconds you get


01:37:49.238 --> 01:37:50.990
before you must be wet.


01:37:51.073 --> 01:37:52.825
You think he said that
or he said that? Four?


01:37:52.909 --> 01:37:56.120
I got to admit, I haven't been sleeping.
I'm just so tired.


01:37:56.203 --> 01:37:57.872
I don't care. I'm about
to be lit on fire!


01:37:57.955 --> 01:38:00.332
He said it! He said what he said.


01:38:00.417 --> 01:38:04.336
Okay, here we go. Right calf first.


01:38:04.421 --> 01:38:06.589
Okay. Okay.


01:38:06.672 --> 01:38:09.008
- Okay!
- Okay, go, go, go!


01:38:09.092 --> 01:38:10.968
Whoo! Yeah!


01:38:12.386 --> 01:38:14.346
...What? Oh!


01:38:15.097 --> 01:38:16.641
No!


01:38:19.351 --> 01:38:21.145
No!


01:38:22.146 --> 01:38:25.900
Okay. So birds sleep at night,
but the bats wake up.


01:38:25.983 --> 01:38:27.569
Okay.


01:38:27.652 --> 01:38:30.947
Now we know. Now we know.
No, this is a good thing.


01:38:34.951 --> 01:38:37.286
I'm telling you, Bud,
he can follow anybody.


01:38:37.369 --> 01:38:40.540
He can follow... He followed Minnie
at The Ice House recently.


01:38:40.623 --> 01:38:44.376
I know you don't like The Ice House.
I don't know why I said that. I'm sorry.


01:38:44.461 --> 01:38:46.128
All right, I'm gonna go watch Kevin.


01:38:46.754 --> 01:38:48.673
- Hey, Sandy.
- Kirby.


01:38:48.756 --> 01:38:49.757
You got a minute?


01:38:49.841 --> 01:38:52.635
Yeah, I'm going to watch
my client on stage.


01:38:52.719 --> 01:38:55.387
Actually, Kevin and I think
it's time for a change.


01:38:55.472 --> 01:38:56.931
He's dumping me through you?


01:38:57.014 --> 01:38:59.601
You gotta admit, you've been
a bit clingy. I'm telling ya.


01:38:59.684 --> 01:39:01.018
You're telling me? I'm telling you.


01:39:01.102 --> 01:39:02.186
So we agree.


01:39:03.605 --> 01:39:07.233
Bud, Alex, how are you guys?
Good to see you.


01:39:07.316 --> 01:39:09.318
It's all happening
here tonight, isn't it?


01:39:15.116 --> 01:39:19.161
♪ You give me butterfly, butterflies ♪


01:39:19.245 --> 01:39:21.372
♪ Down in my soul ♪


01:39:22.081 --> 01:39:24.125
♪ Butterflies, butterfly ♪


01:39:24.876 --> 01:39:26.628
Why the hell do you
have me singing that song?


01:39:26.711 --> 01:39:28.379
- They hated it!
- No.


01:39:28.462 --> 01:39:29.922
This is an awful idea, Sandy!


01:39:30.006 --> 01:39:33.217
No, I... I'm telling you,
you did better than you think!


01:39:33.300 --> 01:39:36.262
- You are out of your mind!
- No! No!


01:39:36.345 --> 01:39:37.805
- I'm sorry.
- No, don't.


01:39:37.889 --> 01:39:40.016
- It's time you go night-night.
- No night-night! No!


01:39:40.099 --> 01:39:42.434
- You're fired.
- Oh, God! Come on!


01:39:42.519 --> 01:39:45.897
No! You can't do that to me! Aah!


01:39:48.566 --> 01:39:50.234
We're done, Sandy. We're done!


01:39:50.317 --> 01:39:51.402
Don't say that.


01:39:56.783 --> 01:39:58.576
Your life is an adventure.


01:39:58.660 --> 01:40:00.286
You don't want to miss a single moment.


01:40:00.369 --> 01:40:03.414
- This girl's the new Grace Kelly.
- Now, you don't have to.


01:40:03.497 --> 01:40:07.835
Vag-Eze, America's number one
vaginal discharge ointment.


01:40:07.919 --> 01:40:10.672
Side effects include dryness,
burning, itching, fallopian tube...


01:40:10.755 --> 01:40:13.591
- What's vaginal discharge?
- Can I have some?


01:40:14.175 --> 01:40:17.094
You said it was
a coffee commercial, Sandy!


01:40:18.971 --> 01:40:21.140
What the hell is going on here?


01:40:24.310 --> 01:40:28.064
Please, God, I need a miracle.


01:40:38.282 --> 01:40:44.789
"Remember, kids,
if you laugh when you are blue,


01:40:44.872 --> 01:40:46.958
the sun...


01:40:47.041 --> 01:40:50.127
...will always shine on you.


01:40:51.420 --> 01:40:54.298
Honk, honk.


01:40:55.883 --> 01:40:58.469
Mr. Buttons."


01:41:29.250 --> 01:41:30.251
Teddy!


01:41:31.794 --> 01:41:35.256
Wonderful news. Mr. Buttons is dead!


01:41:36.758 --> 01:41:38.259
You killed him?


01:41:38.342 --> 01:41:41.470
No! He hung himself!


01:41:41.553 --> 01:41:44.641
- Really?
- His time slot's open, guys.


01:41:44.724 --> 01:41:46.267
I got you the audition.


01:41:46.350 --> 01:41:48.853
It doesn't feel right.
I mean, I feel bad for the guy.


01:41:48.936 --> 01:41:50.938
Screw Mr. Buttons! It's our turn!


01:41:51.022 --> 01:41:55.109
- He couldn't take the pressure.
- He took the coward's way out.


01:41:55.192 --> 01:41:59.446
I gotta tell you, it's the first time
I... I agree with the puppets.


01:42:03.575 --> 01:42:06.203
Friend Boom Boom is gonna
sing a song for us today, kids.


01:42:06.287 --> 01:42:07.830
Would you like that?
Would you like to hear it?


01:42:09.623 --> 01:42:10.875
I hate singing.


01:42:10.958 --> 01:42:13.419
What are you talking about?
You sing all the time.


01:42:13.502 --> 01:42:15.838
You sing in the car,
you sing in the shower...


01:42:15.922 --> 01:42:17.674
You spy on me in the shower?


01:42:19.133 --> 01:42:22.178
- That is not what I meant.
- I can sing, Ted.


01:42:22.261 --> 01:42:25.431
- Would you like to hear that, kids?
- Yeah!


01:42:31.478 --> 01:42:33.189
You have something
in your throat, Heather?


01:42:33.272 --> 01:42:34.565
Yeah, your hand, dummy!


01:42:38.485 --> 01:42:41.030
I can't believe it.
These kids are eating your boy up!


01:42:41.113 --> 01:42:42.573
I mean, he could be the next Buttons.


01:42:42.656 --> 01:42:44.909
- Didn't I tell you? Didn't I say?
- Yeah, great.


01:42:44.992 --> 01:42:47.536
Hey! There's a caterpillar on your face.


01:42:48.788 --> 01:42:50.372
What's with you?
What, are you okay?


01:42:50.456 --> 01:42:53.084
- No, no, I, uh...
- Something wrong? There's something wrong?


01:42:53.167 --> 01:42:56.462
Maybe a little dizzy.
I had too many bacon bits this morning.


01:42:56.545 --> 01:42:59.548
Bacon Bits? What is that?
That's a dog food, no?


01:42:59.631 --> 01:43:01.801
No. Didn't say that on the box.


01:43:01.884 --> 01:43:05.346
Yeah, all right, whatever. Tell you what,
you come to my office in an hour.


01:43:05.429 --> 01:43:06.889
We'll hammer out a deal.


01:43:06.973 --> 01:43:10.059
I'll get your boy on the air ASAP.
Okay, bud?


01:43:10.142 --> 01:43:13.062
All righty. That makes me very happy.


01:43:15.606 --> 01:43:17.316
They absolutely loved you.


01:43:17.399 --> 01:43:19.902
- You're getting the job, Teddy.
- I did good. I did good.


01:43:19.986 --> 01:43:23.697
My only fear is they're gonna try
to lowball you on the deal, all right?


01:43:23.781 --> 01:43:26.242
The key to this meeting is tough talk.


01:43:26.909 --> 01:43:30.913
These TV jerks only respond
to bullying and aggression.


01:43:30.997 --> 01:43:33.540
Well, I'll let you
handle all that, okay?


01:43:35.001 --> 01:43:38.545
I'm no doctor,
but Sandy look like crap on a stick.


01:43:38.629 --> 01:43:40.172
No, I'm fine.


01:43:40.256 --> 01:43:42.674
- Sandy!
- No.


01:43:42.759 --> 01:43:44.718
I think he's having a heart attack.


01:43:44.802 --> 01:43:47.679
We... we gotta get you to a hospital.
Boom Boom, call an ambulance!


01:43:47.764 --> 01:43:54.186
No, Boom Boom. First meeting,
close deal, then hop-ital.


01:43:54.270 --> 01:43:56.438
Forget the meeting.
You can barely speak.


01:43:57.064 --> 01:44:00.401
But... you can.


01:44:03.863 --> 01:44:07.950
So what we saw in there
told us everything we need to know.


01:44:08.617 --> 01:44:11.412
We love Ted. The kids love Ted.


01:44:11.495 --> 01:44:13.122
That is... That's spectacular.


01:44:13.205 --> 01:44:14.748
Thank you.
Thank you so much.


01:44:14.832 --> 01:44:17.919
But the fact is
he's never been on television.


01:44:18.002 --> 01:44:19.670
So here's the deal.


01:44:19.753 --> 01:44:24.801
Six episodes, 15 grand a pop,
and then we see what we do from there.


01:44:31.307 --> 01:44:33.350
Are you kidding me, Marty?


01:44:34.601 --> 01:44:38.189
- What?
- You think I'm a complete a-hole?


01:44:38.272 --> 01:44:39.648
No, no, no.


01:44:39.731 --> 01:44:42.193
Then why are you treating me like one?


01:44:42.776 --> 01:44:45.529
I think it's a reasonable
starting place, Sandy.


01:44:47.239 --> 01:44:50.617
Reasonable, Fishbein? It's dog crap.


01:44:51.202 --> 01:44:52.536
If we take this deal,


01:44:52.619 --> 01:44:56.833
my guy's gonna end up at the end of
a rope just like your last clown.


01:44:57.458 --> 01:44:59.668
- Whoa, man!
- All right. Sandy, Sandy. Take it easy.


01:44:59.751 --> 01:45:02.546
Take it easy. Just make us a counter.


01:45:03.923 --> 01:45:07.969
We want a two year...
Five year deal.


01:45:08.052 --> 01:45:09.136
Sandy, please.


01:45:09.220 --> 01:45:13.057
Twenty-four show minimum,
50 grand an episode,


01:45:13.140 --> 01:45:17.728
with a 200K bump
every year we're on the air.


01:45:18.395 --> 01:45:20.022
This guy's an animal.


01:45:20.106 --> 01:45:21.648
He's literally foaming at the mouth.


01:45:21.732 --> 01:45:24.818
And the puppets get
their own dressing rooms.


01:45:27.113 --> 01:45:28.197
Just kidding.


01:45:29.365 --> 01:45:30.491
Okay.


01:45:30.574 --> 01:45:34.703
Three years, 20 show minimum,
at the numbers you mentioned.


01:45:35.746 --> 01:45:36.788
Deal.


01:45:36.873 --> 01:45:40.584
Ted, welcome to the UPN family.


01:45:46.798 --> 01:45:52.304
And that's how Sandy died.
On the conference room floor at UPN.


01:45:54.056 --> 01:45:55.975
Just kidding.
They took him to the hospital.


01:45:57.434 --> 01:45:58.853
Where am I?


01:45:58.936 --> 01:46:01.898
You had a minor heart attack.
A warning shot.


01:46:02.606 --> 01:46:05.109
Probably due to stress. And meat.


01:46:05.192 --> 01:46:08.237
Just need to rest for a few days.
Here you go.


01:46:13.700 --> 01:46:18.872
This is too nice of a room for me.
I can't afford this.


01:46:18.956 --> 01:46:23.002
Come on, man. I wasn't gonna let you
slum it down in the regular people ward.


01:46:23.085 --> 01:46:25.796
First class all the way for my Sandman.


01:46:25.879 --> 01:46:28.340
- You came!
- Of course.


01:46:28.424 --> 01:46:30.842
Miss Clarke, I love your new album.


01:46:30.927 --> 01:46:32.511
I play it every day.
I'm obsessed with it.


01:46:32.594 --> 01:46:33.595
Thank you.


01:46:33.679 --> 01:46:34.888
- You're so beautiful.
- Thank you.


01:46:34.972 --> 01:46:37.016
Can I touch you?


01:46:38.767 --> 01:46:41.395
Oh, I... I...
I just touched the queen!


01:46:41.478 --> 01:46:45.357
Oh, and you, sir, you need a new bedpan,
so I'm gonna grab that for you.


01:46:45.441 --> 01:46:48.319
- I used the bedpan while I was sleeping?
- Thanks.


01:46:49.903 --> 01:46:51.822
You did a new album?


01:46:51.905 --> 01:46:55.534
Oh. Don't you worry about that. I want
you to worry about getting better.


01:46:56.243 --> 01:46:59.371
It's scary, knowing
your heart's not good.


01:46:59.455 --> 01:47:04.668
Sandy Wexler, you have
the biggest, best, strongest heart


01:47:04.751 --> 01:47:08.422
in this whole miserable town.
And that's a fact.


01:47:08.505 --> 01:47:10.216
Miserable town?


01:47:10.299 --> 01:47:13.594
It's been quite nice to you,
thank you very much.


01:47:13.677 --> 01:47:14.971
I guess.


01:47:15.054 --> 01:47:17.264
I just feel like I need a change,
you know?


01:47:19.016 --> 01:47:20.892
So I'm moving to Seattle.


01:47:20.977 --> 01:47:23.895
Seattle? What are you talking about?


01:47:23.980 --> 01:47:30.277
That whole grunge thing, that's old hat.
Why would you go there?


01:47:31.195 --> 01:47:34.865
The guy I'm marrying lives there.


01:47:37.743 --> 01:47:39.328
You're getting married?


01:47:41.080 --> 01:47:42.498
Yeah.


01:47:42.581 --> 01:47:44.750
Saturday, in Malibu.


01:47:44.833 --> 01:47:48.462
His name is Eric Lamonsoff.
He's not in show business.


01:47:48.545 --> 01:47:50.964
He owns a chain of coffee stores.


01:47:51.048 --> 01:47:54.593
A store that just sells coffee?
I don't know.


01:47:54.676 --> 01:47:56.720
That ain't gonna work, kid.


01:47:57.554 --> 01:48:00.557
I just need a... a break from the music.


01:48:01.142 --> 01:48:05.021
But singing's the only thing
that makes you happy.


01:48:05.104 --> 01:48:08.357
Yeah, but I'm looking for something else
to make me happy.


01:48:10.484 --> 01:48:11.902
'Cause that's not it anymore.


01:48:15.239 --> 01:48:18.784
Miss Clarke, I'm so sorry to bother you,
but would you?


01:48:18.867 --> 01:48:20.119
Sure.


01:48:20.202 --> 01:48:22.913
Is that the record? Can you play it?


01:48:22.996 --> 01:48:25.041
- Is there a player in the room?
- Yeah.


01:48:26.083 --> 01:48:27.959
I gotta hear this.


01:48:34.841 --> 01:48:36.718
You were always there for me.


01:48:39.430 --> 01:48:40.764
Even when you weren't.


01:48:49.606 --> 01:48:50.982
Goodbye, Sandy.


01:49:00.617 --> 01:49:04.413
♪ My world had no room for dreams ♪


01:49:04.496 --> 01:49:06.832
♪ When you found me ♪


01:49:08.625 --> 01:49:11.878
♪ I was happy just floating downstream ♪


01:49:11.962 --> 01:49:15.882
♪ That's when you found me ♪


01:49:16.758 --> 01:49:21.388
♪ Life was passing me by
But you told me to fly ♪


01:49:21.472 --> 01:49:24.683
♪ I thought that I was invisible ♪


01:49:24.766 --> 01:49:28.687
♪ But you saw me ♪


01:49:28.770 --> 01:49:35.236
♪ Yeah, you saw me ♪


01:49:35.819 --> 01:49:39.698
♪ And I'm gonna love you ♪


01:49:39.781 --> 01:49:43.869
♪ In the rain or shine
Till the end of time ♪


01:49:43.952 --> 01:49:47.956
♪ Let you know that I need you ♪


01:49:48.039 --> 01:49:52.586
♪ You're my everything
The reason I sing ♪


01:49:52.669 --> 01:49:56.132
♪ Just take me away
Give me love ♪


01:49:56.215 --> 01:49:59.718
♪ The northern lights
And the stars above... ♪


01:49:59.801 --> 01:50:02.804
♪ ...went wandering far and near ♪


01:50:02.888 --> 01:50:07.100
♪ But in every place
They said to his face now ♪


01:50:07.184 --> 01:50:09.353
♪ Get out of here ♪


01:50:09.936 --> 01:50:12.564
♪ Get out, get out ♪


01:50:12.648 --> 01:50:14.233
I love this song.


01:50:14.858 --> 01:50:16.402
This guy's butchering it.


01:50:19.780 --> 01:50:20.864
Alfred?


01:50:22.241 --> 01:50:24.993
Wow. Nobody's called me that in years.


01:50:25.994 --> 01:50:27.329
Good to see you, Sandy.


01:50:27.413 --> 01:50:30.081
Hey, what are you doing here?


01:50:30.166 --> 01:50:32.626
Well, this is where
I get all my best ideas.


01:50:32.709 --> 01:50:34.127
Well, here and the radio.


01:50:34.211 --> 01:50:36.922
Yeah, you... you've been on such a roll.


01:50:37.005 --> 01:50:40.842
From "My Bologna"
to "Pretty Fly for a Rabbi."


01:50:40.926 --> 01:50:42.969
Just great. Clever stuff.


01:50:43.053 --> 01:50:45.681
Oh, thanks, man. Well, you know,
you're the one who put it all together.


01:50:45.764 --> 01:50:47.724
...Remember what you told me?


01:50:47.808 --> 01:50:49.268
- Stick with the accordion.
- Uh-huh.


01:50:49.351 --> 01:50:51.270
Only wear Hawaiian shirts.


01:50:51.353 --> 01:50:54.022
Do funny words to other people's songs.


01:50:54.105 --> 01:50:55.399
- Genius.
- Huh?


01:50:55.482 --> 01:50:59.611
I'm glad. I'm glad it all worked out
for you. I really am. Sincerely.


01:50:59.695 --> 01:51:03.490
Thank you, man. Well, I'm just sorry
that we couldn't have done it together.


01:51:04.074 --> 01:51:05.992
Hey, listen. I got too close.


01:51:06.076 --> 01:51:08.745
Our friendship was getting
in the way of our business.


01:51:08.829 --> 01:51:10.706
You did what you had to do.


01:51:10.789 --> 01:51:13.834
Wait a minute.
Is that what you think happened?


01:51:13.917 --> 01:51:15.168
That is what happened.


01:51:15.252 --> 01:51:17.921
- You thought we got too close?
- Yeah.


01:51:18.004 --> 01:51:20.632
- No, Sandy.
- That's not why I left you.


01:51:20.716 --> 01:51:24.052
I left you because you
could never tell me the truth.


01:51:24.720 --> 01:51:26.347
What? That's ridiculous!


01:51:26.430 --> 01:51:29.015
Tell me one time
I didn't tell you the truth.


01:51:30.434 --> 01:51:33.061
You told me we could copyright
the word "weird."


01:51:33.144 --> 01:51:36.857
No, I said it was weird
that we couldn't copyright it.


01:51:36.940 --> 01:51:39.651
You... Come on. You were hearing
what you want to hear.


01:51:39.735 --> 01:51:42.070
Sandy, you tell people
what you think they want to hear.


01:51:42.153 --> 01:51:44.656
- I don't agree.
- No, look.


01:51:44.740 --> 01:51:50.537
For me, if you really care about
someone, you tell 'em the truth.


01:51:59.630 --> 01:52:01.047
You're right, Alfred.


01:52:02.508 --> 01:52:04.426
Damn it, you're 100% right.


01:52:05.969 --> 01:52:08.972
- Your hair looks good, by the way.
- Thanks, man, I...


01:52:09.848 --> 01:52:13.310
- You're lying again.
- I am. It looks like dirty spaghetti.


01:52:13.394 --> 01:52:16.062
I gotta stop. I'm gonna stop!


01:52:16.146 --> 01:52:18.023
- I'm gonna stop, Alfred.
- You should.


01:52:22.403 --> 01:52:25.614
Hey! Hey! You suck!


01:52:25.697 --> 01:52:28.284
You know what?
Real funny, Weird Al.


01:52:28.367 --> 01:52:32.371
Why don't you make me laugh one time
without using somebody else's music?


01:52:32.454 --> 01:52:33.580
Get off of me.


01:52:34.831 --> 01:52:38.168
I'd like to book a space
for a private event.


01:52:38.251 --> 01:52:42.714
No! No! Don't tell me it's impossible!
Everything's negotiable!


01:52:48.304 --> 01:52:51.515
Put it on your calendar, Ted.
Okay? Don't be late.


01:52:51.598 --> 01:52:53.058
I think we'll be busy.


01:52:53.141 --> 01:52:54.435
- I'm not talking to you.
- Hey!


01:52:54.518 --> 01:52:55.644
I'm talking to Ted!


01:52:55.727 --> 01:52:57.938
- Okay. We'll be there.
- What's his problem?


01:52:58.021 --> 01:52:59.773
I don't know. Just do what he says.


01:53:09.366 --> 01:53:12.786
It's an international call,
so talk fast, okay?


01:53:13.537 --> 01:53:14.746
Can I count on you?


01:53:15.789 --> 01:53:16.790
Perfect.


01:53:16.873 --> 01:53:18.709
And you have a valid driver's license?


01:53:23.380 --> 01:53:24.631
How am I looking?


01:53:24.715 --> 01:53:26.174
You actually look good, Sandy.


